{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-16045429", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2007.02873 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2007.02873 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- Diboson (WW, WZ, ZZ) background modelling uncertainty\n- Finite simulated MC sample size (Barlow-Beeston-like) uncertainty\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- Jet energy scale and resolution uncertainty\n- Lepton reconstruction, identification, isolation, and trigger efficiency uncertainty\n- Missing transverse momentum (E_T^miss) scale, resolution, and trigger uncertainty\n- Multi-jet background estimate uncertainty (1-lepton channel)\n- Pileup modeling uncertainty\n- Signal modelling uncertainty (scale, PDF+alphaS, PS/UE, cross-section, branching fraction)\n- Single-top ($tW$) cross-section, DR/DS scheme, PS/hadronisation, and ISR/FSR uncertainty\n- Statistical uncertainty of eμ control-region data (data-driven ttbar estimate, 2-lepton channel)\n- W+jets background modelling uncertainty (normalisation, shape, acceptance)\n- Z+jets background modelling uncertainty (normalisation, shape, acceptance)\n- b-tagging efficiency correction-factor uncertainty\n- ttbar background modelling uncertainty (normalisation, flavour composition, shape)\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the analysis.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.03799", "2103.04956", "2103.06956", "2106.01676", "2109.13808", "2111.08340", "2112.00895", "2112.03161", "2202.08676", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2307.01094", "2309.14442", "2401.05299", "2402.08486", "2407.10549", "2503.19420", "2506.13565", "2508.13900", "2510.07527", "2604.21670", "2605.14245"], "v