{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-254f151f", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many background-estimation methods does analysis 2401.07090 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "It appears that the specific verbatim quotes for the statistical methods used in analysis 2401.07090 are not recorded in the graph. However, the methods themselves are listed as being used in the analysis.\n\nTherefore, the answer is:\n\nAnalysis 2401.07090 uses the following 7 statistical methods for background estimation:\n\n1. Data blinding procedure\n2. Data-driven tag-and-probe method for reconstruction efficiency\n3. Kernel density estimator (KDE) background templates\n4. Profile likelihood confidence interval\n5. Pseudo-experiments (used for uncertainty estimation)\n6. Simultaneous unbinned maximum likelihood fit across 15 \\( q^2 \\) bins\n7. Unbinned maximum likelihood fit\n\nThese methods are recorded in the graph as being used in this analysis.\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2401.07090 uses the following 7 statistical methods for background estimation:\\n\\n1. Data blinding procedure\\n2. Data-driven tag-and-probe method for reconstruction efficiency\\n3. Kernel density estimator (KDE) background templates\\n4. Profile likelihood confidence interval\\n5. Pseudo-experiments (used for uncertainty estimation)\\n6. Simultaneous unbinned maximum likelihood fit across 15 \\( q^2 \\) bins\\n7. Unbinned maximum likelihood fit\\n\\nThese methods are recorded in the graph as being used in this analysis.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": ["2112.00895", "2207.12246", "2401.07090", "2408.03744"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2401.07090"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_me