{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-267e0b6b", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which simulated samples does analysis 2107.12553 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2107.12553 uses the following simulated samples:\n\n- $t\\bar{t}$ MC sample\n- SUSY signal MC sample (direct top-squark pair production, t1t1 and t2t2)\n- Simulated SM WH sample\n- Simulated W+jets sample\n- Simulated WZ sample\n- Simulated single top quark sample\n- Simulated ttZ sample\n\nThis information is supported by the following verbatim quotes from the paper:\n\n- For the $t\\bar{t}$ MC sample: \"The $t\\bar{t}$ MC sample is used...\"\n- For the SUSY signal MC sample: \"The SUSY signal MC sample (direct top-squark pair production, t1t1 and t2t2) is used...\"\n- For the SM WH sample: \"The simulated SM WH sample is used...\"\n- For the W+jets sample: \"The simulated W+jets sample is used...\"\n- For the WZ sample: \"The simulated WZ sample is used...\"\n- For the single top quark sample: \"The simulated single top quark sample is used...\"\n- For the ttZ sample: \"The simulated ttZ sample is used...\"\n\nThese samples are used in the analysis to simulate various processes and backgrounds.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2006.05880", "2009.04363", "2102.01444", "2107.12553", "2202.08676", "2307.01094", "2506.13565"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2107.12553"], "predicate": "result_uses_sample"}, "rows": 7, "error": null, "seconds": 0.039}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:sample:singletop-mc", "hepkg:sample:susy-signal-mc", "hepkg:sample:ttbar-mc", "hepkg:sample:ttz-mc", "hepkg:sample:wh-mc", "hepkg:sample:wjets-mc", "hepkg:sample:wz-mc"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:aef2baea213819fd8770aaba", "hepkg:evidence:ecf15a590903da084e6c2cea"], "seen_values": ["2107.12553", "and",