{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-2af8172b", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2004.14060 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2004.14060 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- $b$-tagging efficiency calibration uncertainty\n- Data statistical uncertainty in control regions (background normalisation factors $\\mu_{\\text{bkg}}$)\n- $E_T^{\\text{miss}}$ soft-term energy scale and resolution uncertainty\n- Electron and muon reconstruction/identification uncertainty\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- Jet energy resolution (JER) uncertainty\n- Jet energy scale (JES) uncertainty\n- MC simulation statistical uncertainty\n- Pile-up reweighting modelling uncertainty\n- Signal acceptance theory uncertainty (scale/matching/PS tune variations)\n- Signal total cross-section theory uncertainty\n- Single-top (Wt) modelling uncertainty (diagram removal vs subtraction)\n- Track-jet $b$-tagging performance uncertainty\n- W/Z+jets modelling uncertainty (missing higher orders, scale variations)\n- $t\\bar{t}$ modelling (theory) uncertainty\n- $t\\bar{t}+W/Z$ modelling uncertainty (scale and PS variations)\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the paper with the arXiv ID 2004.14060.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.01581", "2012.03799", "2103.04956", "2106.01676", "2106.14246", "2109.13808", "2111.08340", "2202.08676", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2307.01094", "2309.14442", "2401.05299", "2402.08486", "2407.10549", "2503.19420", "2506.13565", "2510.07527", "2604.21670"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2004.14060"], "predicate": "result_has_systematic"}, "rows