{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-3d259c4f", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which observables does analysis 2401.07090 measure?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2401.07090 measures the following observables:\n\n- Differential branching fraction \\( \\frac{dB(B^+ \\to K^+ \\mu^+ \\mu^-)}{dq^2} \\)\n- Integrated branching fraction \\( B(B^+ \\to K^+ \\mu^+ \\mu^-) \\)\n- Cross-check ratio \\( R(J/\\psi) = \\frac{B(B^+ \\to J/\\psi(\\mu \\mu) K^+)}{B(B^+ \\to J/\\psi(e e) K^+)} \\)\n- Double ratio \\( R(K) = \\frac{B(B^+ \\to K^+ \\mu^+ \\mu^-)}{B(B^+ \\to K^+ e^+ e^-)} \\) (normalized to \\( B^+ \\to J/\\psi K^+ \\) decays)\n- Cross-check ratio \\( R(\\psi(2S)) = \\frac{B(B^+ \\to \\psi(2S)(\\mu \\mu) K^+)}{B(B^+ \\to J/\\psi(\\mu \\mu) K^+)} \\) divided by the \\( e^+ e^- \\) analogue\n- Signal yield from an unbinned maximum likelihood fit to \\( K^+ \\ell^+ \\ell^- \\) invariant mass\n- Single ratio \\( \\frac{B(B^+ \\to K^+ \\ell^+ \\ell^-)}{B(B^+ \\to J/\\psi(\\ell^+ \\ell^-) K^+)} \\)\n\nThese observables are recorded in the paper with the arXiv ID 2401.07090.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2401.07090"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2401.07090"], "predicate": "result_measures_observable"}, "rows": 7, "error": null, "seconds": 0.038}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:observable:diff_bf_dq2", "hepkg:observable:int_bf", "hepkg:observable:r_jpsi_obs", "hepkg:observable:r_psi2s_obs", "hepkg:observable:rk", "hepkg:observable:signal_yield", "hepkg:observable:single_ratio"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:0627bc04d66091a8162278bc", "hepkg:evidence:311393141854102c37c811b3", "hepkg:evidence:4582946dc07c134287337e9f", "hepkg:evidence:7f894481299262301e729668", "hepkg:evidence:830d04e00c10e61afeb42faa", "hepkg:evidence:a0c925c4273e7f146a36146e", "h