{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-4108a111", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2009.04363 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2009.04363 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- Bias from choice of parametric background function\n- ECAL L1 trigger timing shift correction uncertainty (forward endcap)\n- Electron selection efficiency uncertainty\n- Integrated luminosity measurement uncertainty\n- Jet energy scale and resolution uncertainty\n- Muon momentum scale and resolution uncertainty\n- Muon selection and trigger efficiency uncertainty\n- PDF uncertainty\n- Parton shower (ISR/FSR) modelling uncertainty\n- Pileup modelling uncertainty\n- QCD renormalization and factorization scale uncertainty\n- Uncertainty from limited size of simulated samples\n- Uncertainty in prediction of B(H->mu+mu-)\n- VBF signal theoretical modelling uncertainty (pT(H), pT(Hjj), jet multiplicity, mjj)\n- b quark jet identification/veto efficiency uncertainty\n- ggH signal theoretical modelling uncertainty (pT(H), jet multiplicity, VBF contamination)\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the analysis and contribute to the overall systematic uncertainty of the results.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2009.04363", "2403.01556"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2009.04363"], "predicate": "result_has_systematic"}, "rows": 16, "error": null, "seconds": 0.048}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:systematic:b-tagging-veto-efficiency-uncertainty", "hepkg:systematic:background-function-choice-bias", "hepkg:systematic:branching-fraction-uncertainty", "hepkg:systematic:ecal-l1-trigger-timing-uncertainty", "hepkg:systematic:electron-selection-efficiency-uncertainty", "hepkg:systematic:ggh-signal-modeling-uncer