{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-43cc1ae8", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many simulated samples does analysis 2007.02873 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2007.02873 uses 19 simulated samples, including alternative and nominal samples for various processes such as W+HF, Wt, diboson, ttbar, single top, W+jets, Z/γ*→ll, Z→νν, gg→VV, gg→ZH, qq→WH, qq→ZH, and diboson processes (WW, WZ, ZZ). \n\nHere are the specific samples:\n- Alternative W+HF matrix-element sample (MadGraph5_aMC@NLO+Pythia8)\n- Alternative Wt parton-shower sample (Powheg+Herwig++)\n- Alternative diboson sample (Powheg+Herwig++)\n- Alternative diboson sample (Powheg+Pythia8)\n- Alternative ttbar matrix-element sample (MadGraph5_aMC@NLO+Pythia8)\n- Alternative ttbar parton-shower sample (Powheg+Herwig7)\n- Nominal ttbar MC sample (Powheg-Box v2 + Pythia 8.230)\n- Single top quark s-channel background sample\n- Single top quark t-channel background sample\n- W+jets MC sample (Sherpa 2.2.1)\n- Wt single-top MC sample\n- Z/γ*→ll MC sample (Sherpa 2.2.1)\n- Z→νν MC sample (Sherpa 2.2.1)\n- gg→VV diboson MC sample (Sherpa 2.2.2)\n- gg→ZH signal MC sample\n- qq→WH signal MC sample\n- qq→WW diboson MC sample (Sherpa 2.2.1)\n- qq→WZ diboson MC sample (Sherpa 2.2.1)\n- qq→ZH signal MC sample\n- qq→ZZ diboson MC sample (Sherpa 2.2.1)\n\nThis information is based on the records in the graph.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2007.02873 uses 19 simulated samples, including alternative and nominal samples for various processes such as W+HF, Wt, diboson, ttbar, single top, W+jets, Z/γ*→ll, Z→νν, gg→VV, gg→ZH, qq→WH, qq→ZH, and diboson processes (WW, WZ, ZZ).\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}", "answered": true, "papers": ["2007.02873", "2402.08486"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round":