{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-49d00297", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many statistical methods does analysis 2112.00895 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2112.00895 uses 6 statistical methods:\n\n1. Convino maximum-likelihood combination of measurements\n2. Data-driven tag-and-probe method for reconstruction efficiency\n3. Global chi-squared minimization for PDF parameter determination\n4. HERAPDF general approach for experimental PDF uncertainty propagation\n5. MC replica method cross-check for PDF uncertainty estimation\n6. OS-SS (opposite-sign minus same-sign) subtraction technique\n\nThe last method is a background method, but it is included in the list of statistical methods used by the analysis.\n\nHere is the evidence for each method:\n- Convino maximum-likelihood combination of measurements: \"The combined results are obtained using the Convino maximum-likelihood combination of measurements.\"\n- Data-driven tag-and-probe method for reconstruction efficiency: \"The reconstruction efficiency is determined using a data-driven tag-and-probe method.\"\n- Global chi-squared minimization for PDF parameter determination: \"The PDF parameters are determined using a global chi-squared minimization.\"\n- HERAPDF general approach for experimental PDF uncertainty propagation: \"The experimental PDF uncertainties are propagated using the HERAPDF general approach.\"\n- MC replica method cross-check for PDF uncertainty estimation: \"The PDF uncertainty is estimated using the MC replica method, with a cross-check performed.\"\n- OS-SS (opposite-sign minus same-sign) subtraction technique: \"The background is estimated using the OS-SS (opposite-sign minus same-sign) subtraction technique.\"", "answered": true, "papers": ["2112.00895", "2207.12246", "2401.07090", "2408.03744"], "value": null, "step