{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-5149e13d", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many background-estimation methods does analysis 2509.22535 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2509.22535 uses two background-estimation methods:\n\n1. **Control-region-based normalization fit for \\( t\\bar{t} \\)+jets components**\n2. **Direct simulation estimate assuming SM production rates**\n\nThese methods are used to estimate the background contributions in the analysis. \n\nThis information is supported by the following verbatim quotes from the paper:\n\n- For the control-region-based normalization fit: \"Control-region-based normalization fit for \\( t\\bar{t} \\)+jets components.\"\n- For the direct simulation estimate: \"Direct simulation estimate assuming SM production rates.\"\n\nTherefore, the analysis 2509.22535 uses **2** background-estimation methods.\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"The analysis 2509.22535 uses 2 background-estimation methods: 1. Control-region-based normalization fit for \\( t\\\\bar{t} \\\\)+jets components 2. Direct simulation estimate assuming SM production rates. These methods are used to estimate the background contributions in the analysis.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": ["2106.14246", "2509.22535"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2509.22535"], "predicate": "background_uses_method"}, "rows": 2, "error": null, "seconds": 0.042}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:control_region_normalization_fit", "hepkg:method:simulation_sm_rate_estimate"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:448c4f4ce3eb4a4adeb371d3", "hepkg:evidence:9ece0f43f6c75458af788fa7"], "seen_values": ["2509.22535", "assuming", "background_method", "background_uses_method", "bar", "components", "control-region-based", "direct", "estimate", "fit", "for", "hepkg:method:control_region_normalization_fit", "hepkg:method:simulation_sm_rate_estimate", "jets", "normalization", "production", "rates", "simulation"], "verification_score": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": [], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 6999, "completion_tokens": 284, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 12.493278224952519, "error": ""}, "scores": {"seconds": 12.493278224952519, "llm_calls": 2.0, "tokens": 7283.0, "rounds": 2.0, "errored": 0.0, "answered": 1.0, "abstained": 0.0, "refused_in_text": 0.0, "refusal_flag_disagrees": 0.0, "faithfulness": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": 0.0, "count_correct": 1.0, "tool_calls": 1.0, "tool_errors": 0.0, "tool_error_rate": 0.0, "retrieved_first": 1.0, "entities_retrieved": 2.0, "evidence_quotes": 2.0}}
{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-5252cb5b", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2307.01094 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2307.01094 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- $E_{\\text{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ scale/resolution and soft-term uncertainty\n- 50% overall cross-section uncertainty assigned to rarer background processes not computed in detail\n- Charge-flip electron background prediction uncertainty (~50% typical, from $\\gamma$ correction measurement)\n- Fake/non-prompt lepton estimate systematic uncertainty (matrix-method $\\varepsilon$/$\\zeta$ extrapolation and contamination)\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- Jet uncertainties: JVT, jet energy scale (JES), jet energy resolution (JER), flavour tagging\n- Lepton reconstruction/identification/isolation/energy-scale/resolution/trigger efficiency uncertainties\n- Limited MC simulation sample-size statistical uncertainty\n- Pileup modeling uncertainty\n- Theoretical modelling uncertainties: renormalisation/factorisation/resummation/merging scales, PDF choice (MMHT2014, CT14, NNPDF), and cross-section normalisation\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the analysis.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.03799", "2103.04956", "2106.01676", "2109.13808", "2111.08340", "2112.03161", "2202.08676", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2307.01094", "2401.05299", "2402.08486", "2407.10549", "2503.19420", "2506.13565", "2508.13900", "2510.07527", "2604.21670"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2307.01094"], "predicate": "result_has_systematic"}, "rows": 10, "error": null, "seconds": 0.047}], "sets": {}, "