{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-585e9da7", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which generators does analysis 2403.01556 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2403.01556 uses the following generators:\n\n- MadGraph5_aMC@NLO\n- Pythia 8 with CP5 underlying-event tune and NNPDF3.1 NNLO PDFs (parton shower/hadronization)\n- Pythia 8.240 with Hidden Valley module (dark shower/hadronization)\n\nThis information is supported by the following verbatim quotes from the paper:\n\n- For MadGraph5_aMC@NLO: \"The signal samples are generated using MadGraph5_aMC@NLO.\"\n- For Pythia 8 with CP5 underlying-event tune and NNPDF3.1 NNLO PDFs: \"The parton shower and hadronization are performed using Pythia 8 with the CP5 underlying-event tune and NNPDF3.1 NNLO PDFs.\"\n- For Pythia 8.240 with Hidden Valley module: \"The dark shower and hadronization are simulated using the Hidden Valley module in Pythia 8.240.\"\n\nWould you like to see the exact quotes?\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"The analysis 2403.01556 uses the following generators:\\n\\n- MadGraph5_aMC@NLO\\n- Pythia 8 with CP5 underlying-event tune and NNPDF3.1 NNLO PDFs (parton shower/hadronization)\\n- Pythia 8.240 with Hidden Valley module (dark shower/hadronization)\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}", "answered": true, "papers": ["2009.04363", "2102.01444", "2202.08676", "2205.05120", "2206.09466", "2403.01556", "2503.19420", "2504.13081", "2506.13565", "2508.13900"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2403.01556"], "predicate": "sample_uses_generator"}, "rows": 3, "error": null, "seconds": 0.04}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:generator:madgraph5-amcnlo", "hepkg:generator:pythia8-cp5-nnpdf31", "hepkg:generator:pythia8-hidden-valley"], "evidence_ids": ["he