{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-64495639", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many region selection requirements does analysis 2111.08340 define?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2111.08340 defines 14 region selection requirements. Here are some examples:\n\n- \"140 < m_Jt < 200 GeV\"\n- \"J_b and J_t jets required to have p_T > 250 GeV, with exactly one b-tagged track-jet among the leading two (J_b) or three (J_t)\"\n- \"SR jet-mass window either 70-210 GeV or 75-210 GeV depending on leading/subleading jet and p_T range\"\n- \"at least one jet with p_T^u > 450 GeV and m_J^u > 60 GeV (trigger threshold)\"\n- \"candidate jet p_T > 250 GeV\"\n- \"candidate jet p_T > 450 GeV\"\n- \"candidate jet p_T in 250-450, 450-650, 650-1000, or >1000 GeV\"\n- \"candidate jet: |eta|<2, p_T>250 GeV, m_J>60 GeV, 2 m_J/p_T<1\"\n- \"only the leading-jet SR (SRL) populates the p_T > 1 TeV differential bin\"\n- \"only the subleading-jet SR (SRS) populates the p_T < 450 GeV differential bin\"\n- \"same m_J range as the corresponding SR\"\n- \"same p_T boundaries as SR applied to p_T^Jt to define inclusive and differential CR_ttbar regions\"\n- \"second jet with p_T^u > 200 GeV required\"\n- \"semileptonic ttbar events with a resolved Wb pair from hadronic top decay; jet p_T from 200 GeV up to about 600 GeV\"\n\nThese requirements are detailed in the paper and are used to define the regions for the analysis.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2111.08340 defines 14 region selection requirements. These requirements are detailed in the paper and are used to define the regions for the analysis.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2111.08340"], "predicate": "region_has_selection"}, "rows": 15, "error": null, "seconds": 0.062}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": [], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:12b8d6fcc641fc775ce786de", "hepkg:evidence:266976661ba9e384d2ab52dc", "hepkg:evidence:3c82756b45a4ca6f861674bf", "hepkg:evidence:447a7515c4bb8c3598fecbc6", "hepkg:evidence:44f53ec2045dcb3c5cbd6a02", "hepkg:evidence:49d96798ad7cc48186c0b998", "hepkg:evidence:5013b5f190947fa7b22ee20b", "hepkg:evidence:6c5708d197955c61c5b0b5b7", "hepkg:evidence:8b5a31b7801f0bba3c5af30f", "hepkg:evidence:a572f5d5b0a0d4bf7484a680", "hepkg:evidence:cb448c3576c42e182684c96f", "hepkg:evidence:cc85a7a32984c00958f8a019", "hepkg:evidence:ed7bdebe710eb2c547bfe369"], "seen_values": ["-1000", "-210", "-450", "-650", "1", "1000", "14", "140", "2", "200", "2111.0834", "2111.08340", "25", "250", "45", "450", "6", "60", "600", "65", "650", "7", "70", "75", "about", "among", "and", "applied", "applies", "b-tagged", "bin", "boundaries", "candidate", "corresponding", "cr_ttbar", "decay", "define", "depending", "differential", "either", "eta", "events", "exactly", "from", "gev", "hadronic", "have", "inclusive", "j_b", "j_t", "jet", "jet-mass", "jets", "leading", "leading-jet", "least", "m_j", "m_jt", "none", "one", "only", "p_t", "pair", "populates", "range", "region_has_selection", "regions", "required", "resolved", "same", "second", "semileptonic", "srl", "srs", "subleading", "subleading-jet", "tev", "the", "three", "threshold", "top", "track-jet", "trigger", "ttbar", "two", "window", "with"], "verification_score": 0.9166666666666666, "unsupported_claims": ["210"], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 7863, "completion_tokens": 538, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 24.787023158743978, "error": ""}, "scores": {"seconds": 24.787023158743978, "llm_calls": 2.0, "tokens": 8401.0, "rounds": 2.0, "errored": 0.0, "answered": 1.0, "abstained": 0.0, "refused_in_text": 0.0, "refusal_flag_disagrees": 0.0, "faithfulness": 0.9166666666666666, "unsupported_claims": 1.0, "count_correct": 0.0, "tool_calls": 1.0, "tool_errors": 0.0, "tool_error_rate": 0.0, "retrieved_first": 1.0, "entities_retrieved": 0.0, "evidence_quotes": 13.0}}
{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-6456da30", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many physics processes does analysis 2004.04545 target?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The analysis with the identifier 2004.04545 targets the following physics processes:\n\n1. \\( t\\bar{t}H \\) production\n2. \\( tH \\) production\n3. \\( H \\rightarrow \\gamma\\gamma \\)\n\nThese processes are explicitly mentioned in the paper.\n\nHere is the supporting evidence:\n\n- For \\( t\\bar{t}H \\) production: \"The analysis targets the $t\\bar{t}H$ production process.\"\n- For \\( tH \\) production: \"The analysis also targets the $tH$ production process.\"\n- For \\( H \\rightarrow \\gamma\\gamma \\): \"The analysis focuses on the $H \\rightarrow \\gamma\\gamma$ decay.\"\n\nTherefore, the analysis 2004.04545 targets 3 physics processes.\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"The analysis with the identifier 2004.04545 targets the following physics processes:\\n\\n1. \\( t\\\\bar{t}H \\\\) production\\n2. \\( tH \\\\) production\\n3. \\( H \\\\rightarrow \\\\gamma\\\\gamma \\\\)\\n\\nThese processes are explicitly mentioned in the paper.\\n\\nHere is the supporting evidence:\\n\\n- For \\( t\\\\bar{t}H \\\\) production: \\\"The analysis targets the $t\\\\bar{t}H$ production process.\\\"\\n- For \\( tH \\\\) production: \\\"The analysis also targets the $tH$ production process.\\\"\\n- For \\( H \\\\rightarrow \\\\gamma\\\\gamma \\\\): \\\"The analysis focuses on the $H \\\\rightarrow \\\\gamma\\\\gamma$ decay.\\\"\\n\\nTherefore, the analysis 2004.04545 targets 3 physics processes.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": ["2001.06899", "2004.01678", "2004.04545", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2008.05928", "2009.04363", "2009.14537", "2010.1