{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-65fdd3c5", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which observables does analysis 2506.13565 measure?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2506.13565 measures the following observables:\n\n- Dilepton invariant mass (m_ll) spectrum in ee and mumu channels, by b-tagged jet multiplicity.\n- Ratio of differential dilepton production cross sections \\( R(\\mu\\mu/\\text{ee}) \\) vs dilepton mass.\n\nThese details are supported by the following evidence from the paper:\n\n- For the dilepton invariant mass spectrum: \"Dilepton invariant mass (m_ll) spectrum in ee and mumu channels, by b-tagged jet multiplicity.\"\n- For the ratio of differential dilepton production cross sections: \"Ratio of differential dilepton production cross sections R(mumu/ee) vs dilepton mass.\"\n\nAnswered from the graph.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"The analysis 2506.13565 measures the following observables:\\n\\n- Dilepton invariant mass (m_ll) spectrum in ee and mumu channels, by b-tagged jet multiplicity.\\n- Ratio of differential dilepton production cross sections \\( R(\\\\mu\\\\mu/\\\\text{ee}) \\\\) vs dilepton mass.\\n\\nThese details are supported by the following evidence from the paper:\\n\\n- For the dilepton invariant mass spectrum: \\\"Dilepton invariant mass (m_ll) spectrum in ee and mumu channels, by b-tagged jet multiplicity.\\\"\\n- For the ratio of differential dilepton production cross sections: \\\"Ratio of differential dilepton production cross sections R(mumu/ee) vs dilepton mass.\\\"\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}", "answered": true, "papers": ["2506.13565"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2506.13565"], "predicate": "result_measures_observable"}, "rows": 2, "error": null, "seconds": 0.03}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:observable:dilepton-mass-spectrum", "hepkg:observable:lepton-flavor-ratio"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:33b5959fa573a96730fccd73", "hepkg:evidence:bbf77ea26e746ae3fbc86dca", "hepkg:evidence:f9c344cac1472515aa35b415"], "seen_values": ["2506.13565", "and", "b-tagged", "channels", "cross", "differential", "dilepton", "hepkg:observable:dilepton-mass-spectrum", "hepkg:observable:lepton-flavor-ratio", "invariant", "jet", "m_ll", "mass", "multiplicity", "mumu", "observable", "production", "ratio", "result_measures_observable", "sections", "spectrum"], "verification_score": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": [], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 7015, "completion_tokens": 388, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 17.25447498401627, "error": ""}, "scores": {"seconds": 17.25447498401627, "llm_calls": 2.0, "tokens": 7403.0, "rounds": 2.0, "errored": 0.0, "answered": 1.0, "abstained": 0.0, "refused_in_text": 0.0, "refusal_flag_disagrees": 0.0, "faithfulness": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": 0.0, "retrieved_label_recall": 1.0, "retrieved_entities": 2.0, "mentioned_label_recall": 1.0, "truncation_loss_labels": 0.0, "tool_calls": 1.0, "tool_errors": 0.0, "tool_error_rate": 0.0, "retrieved_first": 1.0, "entities_retrieved": 2.0, "evidence_quotes": 3.0}}
{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-665431e3", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many object selection requirements does analysis 2107.12553 define?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2107.12553 defines 14 object selection requirements. Here are some examples:\n\n- \"DeepCSV working point with light/gluon-jet misidentification rate ~1-2%\"\n- \"anti-kT R=0.4, pT > 30 GeV, |eta| < 2.4, DeltaR > 0.4 from isolated leptons\"\n- \"anti-kT R=0.8, pT > 250 GeV, |eta| < 2.4, DeltaR > 0.8 from isolated leptons\"\n- \"b-jet identification efficiency 65-80% for pT 30-400 GeV; charm-jet misid 10-15%\"\n- \"isolation sum < 0.1 x pT and < 6 GeV\"\n- \"isolation sum < 0.2 x lepton pT\"\n- \"mass-decorrelated DeepAK8 discriminator, misid rate ~2.5% for pT 500-700 GeV; efficiency 60-80%\"\n- \"negative vector pT sum of all PF candidates associated with the primary vertex (excluding non-primary-vertex charged hadrons), corrected for jet energy scale\"\n- \"pT > 10 GeV, |eta| < 2.4\"\n- \"pT > 10 GeV, |eta| < 2.4, MVA isolation\"\n- \"pT > 25 GeV (muon) / 30 GeV (electron); |eta| < 2.1 (muon) / 1.44 (electron)\"\n- \"pT > 5 GeV, |eta| < 2.4\"\n- \"relative isolation sum < 10% of lepton pT within pT-dependent cone (min 0.05, max 0.2), and absolute isolation sum < 5 GeV within DeltaR=0.3\"\n\nThese selections are detailed in the paper and are used to define the objects used in the analysis.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2107.12553 defines 14 object selection requirements. These include criteria for jets, leptons, and other detector objects.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2107.12553"], "predicate": "object_has_selection"}, "rows": 