{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-6680f4ac", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many detector objects does analysis 2006.05880 define?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2006.05880 defines 14 detector objects, including control regions, signal regions, and validation regions for various backgrounds and signal hypotheses. \n\nTo provide a few examples:\n- Control region CR^Z_VV for multi-boson background normalisation (3ℓ selection)\n- Signal region SR^Z_1A (3ℓ selection, t̃1→tχ̃2⁰ with χ̃2⁰→h/Zχ̃1⁰, large mass splitting)\n- Validation region VR^Z_1F for fake/non-prompt lepton background\n\nThese regions are used to validate and normalize the background estimates and to define the signal regions for the analysis.\n\nHere is the full list of defined detector objects:\n- Control region CR^Z_VV for multi-boson background normalisation (3ℓ selection)\n- Control region CR^Z_ttZ for ttZ background normalisation (3ℓ selection)\n- Control region CR^h_ttbar for ttbar background normalisation (1ℓ selection)\n- Shape-fit signal region SR^h_1AB overlapping SR^h_1A and SR^h_1B\n- Signal region SR^Z_1A (3ℓ selection, t̃1→tχ̃2⁰ with χ̃2⁰→h/Zχ̃1⁰, large mass splitting)\n- Signal region SR^Z_1B (3ℓ selection, small χ̃2⁰-χ̃1⁰ mass splitting)\n- Signal region SR^Z_2A (3ℓ selection, t̃2→Zt̃1, small mass splitting)\n- Signal region SR^Z_2B (3ℓ selection, t̃2→Zt̃1, large mass splitting)\n- Signal region SR^h_1A (1ℓ selection, small χ̃2⁰-χ̃1⁰ mass splitting)\n- Signal region SR^h_1B (1ℓ selection, large χ̃2⁰-χ̃1⁰ mass splitting)\n- Validation region VR^Z_1F for fake/non-prompt lepton background\n- Validation region VR^Z_2F for fake/non-prompt lepton background (soft lepton regime)\n- Validation region VR^Z_ttZ for ttZ background estimate\n- Validation region VR^{Z,b-tag}_VV for multi-boson background (b-tag veto released)\n- Validation region VR^{Z,n-jet}_VV for multi-boson background (jet multiplicity extrapolation)\n\nThis information is supported by the following assertions from the paper:\n\n- \"Control region CR^Z_VV for multi-boson background normalisation (3ℓ selection)\"\n- \"Control region CR^Z_ttZ for ttZ background normalisation (3ℓ selection)\"\n- \"Control region CR^h_ttbar for ttbar background normalisation (1ℓ selection)\"\n- \"Shape-fit signal region SR^h_1AB overlapping SR^h_1A and SR^h_1B\"\n- \"Signal region SR^Z_1A (3ℓ selection, t̃1→tχ̃2⁰ with χ̃2⁰→h/Zχ̃1⁰, large mass splitting)\"\n- \"Signal region SR^Z_1B (3ℓ selection, small χ̃2⁰-χ̃1⁰ mass splitting)\"\n- \"Signal region SR^Z_2A (3ℓ selection, t̃2→Zt̃1, small mass splitting)\"\n- \"Signal region SR^Z_2B (3ℓ selection, t̃2→Zt̃1, large mass splitting)\"\n- \"Signal region SR^h_", "answered": true, "papers": ["2006.05880"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2006.05880"], "predicate": "result_defines_object"}, "rows": 15, "error": null, "seconds": 0.043}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:object:CR-Z-VV", "hepkg:object:CR-Z-ttZ", "hepkg:object:CR-h-ttbar", "hepkg:object:SR-Z-1A", "hepkg:object:SR-Z-1B", "hepkg:object:SR-Z-2A", "hepkg:object:SR-Z-2B", "hepkg:object:SR-h-1A", "hepkg:object:SR-h-1AB", "hepkg:object:SR-h-1B", "hepkg:object:VR-Z-1F", "hepkg:object:VR-Z-2F", "hepkg:object:VR-Z-VV-btag", "hepkg:object:VR-Z-VV-njet", "hepkg:object:VR-Z-ttZ"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:26d43cec30eb59253563f342", "hepkg:evidence:484db55bca85e64a64b83d28", "hepkg:evidence:bfe51ccfe20cc010e81f7357", "hepkg:evidence:c4348d65898ab3d0c51c194e", "hepkg:evidence:c6260031d0a6ebe63bb28819", "hepkg:evidence:e279034736f9c44283819aee"], "seen_values": ["1", "2", "2006.0588", "2006.05880", "3", "_vv", "and", "b-tag", "background", "control", "detector_object", "estimate", "extrapolation", "fake", "for", "h_1a", "h_1ab", "h_1b", "h_ttbar", "hepkg:object:cr-h-ttbar", "hepkg:object:cr-z