{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-6cf1a653", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which background-estimation methods does analysis 2604.27044 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2604.27044 uses the following background-estimation methods:\n\n- Barlow-Beeston lite technique for binwise statistical uncertainty modeling\n- Binned maximum likelihood fit for SUSY signal strength, background yields and nuisance parameters\n- CMS statistical analysis tool Combine (RooFit/RooStats based)\n- Feldman-Cousins (FC) procedure for coupling modifier interval coverage\n- Fisher F-test for polynomial/basis-function order selection\n- Modified frequentist CLs criterion with asymptotic approximation\n- Profile likelihood ratio test statistic\n- Quantile matching procedure for validation region input feature alignment\n- Saturated chi-square goodness-of-fit test\n- Wilks' theorem asymptotic interpretation of profiled likelihood test statistic\n- k-fold ensembling method for background reweighting DNN variance estimation\n\nThese methods are used to estimate and validate the background in the analysis. \n\nAnswered from the graph.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2604.27044 uses the following background-estimation methods:\\n\\n- Barlow-Beeston lite technique for binwise statistical uncertainty modeling\\n- Binned maximum likelihood fit for SUSY signal strength, background yields and nuisance parameters\\n- CMS statistical analysis tool Combine (RooFit/RooStats based)\\n- Feldman-Cousins (FC) procedure for coupling modifier interval coverage\\n- Fisher F-test for polynomial/basis-function order selection\\n- Modified frequentist CLs criterion with asymptotic approximation\\n- Profile likelihood ratio test statistic\\n- Quantile matching procedure for validation region input feature alignment\\n- Saturated chi-square goodness-of-fit test\\n- Wilks' theorem asymptotic interpretation of profiled likelihood test statistic\\n- k-fold ensembling method for background reweighting DNN variance estimation\\n\\nThese methods are used to estimate and validate the background in the analysis.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": ["2009.04363", "2107.12553", "2209.07327", "2604.27044"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2604.27044"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 11, "error": null, "seconds": 0.031}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:barlow-beeston-lite", "hepkg:method:binned-ml-fit", "hepkg:method:cls-modified-frequentist", "hepkg:method:combine-tool", "hepkg:method:feldman-cousins", "hepkg:method:fisher-f-test", "hepkg:method:k-fold-ensembling", "hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-ratio", "hepkg:method:quantile-matching", "hepkg:method:saturated-chi2-gof", "hepkg:method:wilks-theorem"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:25b18e888c4e90f56dcef547", "hepkg:evidence:3a15e120794603923eefbcc9", "hepkg:evidence:550e96eec6ef23fefe03d485", "hepkg:evidence:8b4a58c182d86297012e147f", "hepkg:evidence:930f2a5792dc8adb98916c79", "hepkg:evidence:d78598762a1718f66ecc3e35", "hepkg:evidence:dff8fe7d31466c47611ed997"], "seen_values": ["2604.27044", "alignment", "analysis", "and", "approximation", "asymptotic", "background", "barlow-beeston", "based", "basis-function", "binned", "binwise", "chi-square", "cls", "cms", "combine", "coupling", "coverage", "criterion", "dnn", "ensembling", "estimation", "f-test", "feature", "feldman-cousins", "fisher", "fit", "for", "frequentist", "goodness-of-fit", "hepkg:method:barlow-beeston-lite", "hepkg:method:binned-ml-fit", "hepkg:method:cls-modified-frequentist", "hepkg:method:combine-tool", "hepkg:method:feldman-cousins", "hepkg:method:fisher-f-test", "hepkg:method:k-fold-ensembling", "hepkg:method:profi