{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-7618b4aa", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many background-estimation methods does analysis 2106.01676 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2106.01676 uses the following 7 statistical methods for background estimation:\n\n1. Background-only fit (CRs only, no signal, floating WZ normalisation)\n2. CLs prescription for 95% CL exclusion limits\n3. Discovery fit for model-independent upper limits on new-physics cross section\n4. Exclusion fit to set 95% CL exclusion limits on target SUSY models\n5. Maximum-likelihood (profile likelihood) fit with Poisson/Gaussian terms and Beeston-Barlow-lite MC-stat nuisances\n6. Profile likelihood method for computing local significance / p0\n7. pyhf-based statistical combination of orthogonal signal regions (validated against HistFitter)\n\nThese methods are recorded in the graph as being used in this analysis. \n\nAnswered from the graph.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2106.01676 uses the following 7 statistical methods for background estimation:\\n\\n1. Background-only fit (CRs only, no signal, floating WZ normalisation)\\n2. CLs prescription for 95% CL exclusion limits\\n3. Discovery fit for model-independent upper limits on new-physics cross section\\n4. Exclusion fit to set 95% CL exclusion limits on target SUSY models\\n5. Maximum-likelihood (profile likelihood) fit with Poisson/Gaussian terms and Beeston-Barlow-lite MC-stat nuisances\\n6. Profile likelihood method for computing local significance / p0\\n7. pyhf-based statistical combination of orthogonal signal regions (validated against HistFitter)\\n\\nThese methods are recorded in the graph as being used in this analysis.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": ["2006.05880", 