{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-7652eebc", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which simulated samples does analysis 2407.10549 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2407.10549 uses the following simulated samples:\n\n- $V$+jets sample (Sherpa 2.2.1)\n- $Vh$ associated production background sample (Powheg Box + Pythia 8.186)\n- $t\\bar{t}$ background sample (Powheg Box v2 + Pythia 8.230)\n- Alternative $V\\!+\\!\\mathrm{jets}$ sample (MadGraph5_aMC@NLO 2.6.2 + Pythia 8.230)\n- Alternative $tW$ single-top sample using diagram subtraction scheme\n- Alternative $t\\bar{t}$ sample for generator systematic (MadGraph5_aMC@NLO 2.6.0 + Pythia 8.230)\n- Alternative $t\\bar{t}$ sample for parton-shower systematic (Powheg Box + Herwig 7.04)\n- Diboson ($VV$) background sample (Sherpa 2.2.1/2.2.2)\n- Pileup overlay sample (Pythia 8.186, A3 tune)\n- Signal MC sample: $pp\\rightarrow Z^{\\prime}\\rightarrow s\\chi\\chi\\rightarrow b\\bar{b}\\chi\\chi$ (MadGraph5_aMC@NLO+Pythia8)\n- Single-top-quark background sample (Powheg Box v2 + Pythia 8.230)\n\nThese samples are used to simulate various backgrounds and signal processes in the analysis.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2010.14293", "2012.03799", "2401.05299", "2407.10549"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2407.10549"], "predicate": "result_uses_sample"}, "rows": 11, "error": null, "seconds": 0.043}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:sample:diboson-sherpa", "hepkg:sample:pileup-pythia", "hepkg:sample:signal-zprime-schichi-mc", "hepkg:sample:singletop-powheg-pythia", "hepkg:sample:singletop-tw-diagram-subtraction", "hepkg:sample:ttbar-alt-mg5-pythia", "hepkg:sample:ttbar-alt-powheg-herwig", "hepkg:sample:ttbar-powheg-pythia", "hepkg:sample:vh-powheg-pythia", "hepkg:sample:vjets-alt-mg5", "hepkg:sample:vjets-sherp