{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-786b9a61", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which statistical methods does analysis 2112.03161 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2112.03161 uses the following statistical methods:\n\n- **2D binned maximum likelihood fit** of \\( m_{bb} \\) and \\( m_{HH} \\) distributions.\n- **Asymptotic approximation of the CLs method** for 95% CL upper limits.\n- **Likelihood ratio goodness-of-fit test** using the saturated model.\n- **Pseudo-experiments** used to validate the asymptotic limit calculation and test signal-fit bias.\n\nThese methods are supported by the following quotes from the paper:\n\n- For the 2D binned maximum likelihood fit: \"A 2D binned maximum likelihood fit of the \\( m_{bb} \\) and \\( m_{HH} \\) distributions is performed.\"\n- For the asymptotic approximation of the CLs method: \"The asymptotic approximation of the CLs method is used to set 95% CL upper limits.\"\n- For the likelihood ratio goodness-of-fit test: \"A likelihood ratio goodness-of-fit test using the saturated model is performed.\"\n- For the pseudo-experiments: \"Pseudo-experiments are used to validate the asymptotic limit calculation and test for signal-fit bias.\"\n\nAnswered from the graph.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2112.03161", "2201.11585"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2112.03161"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 4, "error": null, "seconds": 0.036}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:cls_asymptotic", "hepkg:method:goodness_of_fit_saturated", "hepkg:method:ml_fit_2d", "hepkg:method:pseudoexperiments_crosscheck"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:05c964f0b33167be71d5b7a8", "hepkg:evidence:7dd38e4b699ab3ee943162be", "hepkg:evidence:8b6262f4d7c09fcccd20764c", "hepkg:evidence:bfb3c17c2721c5db0f1