{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-7933ff98", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which statistical methods does analysis 2401.07090 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2401.07090 uses the following statistical methods:\n\n- Data blinding procedure\n- Data-driven tag-and-probe method for reconstruction efficiency\n- Kernel density estimator (KDE) background templates\n- Profile likelihood confidence interval\n- Pseudo-experiments (used for uncertainty estimation)\n- Simultaneous unbinned maximum likelihood fit across 15 \\( q^2 \\) bins\n- Unbinned maximum likelihood fit\n\nThese methods are recorded in the graph based on the statements made in the paper.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2112.00895", "2207.12246", "2401.07090", "2408.03744"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2401.07090"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 7, "error": null, "seconds": 0.038}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:data_blinding", "hepkg:method:kde", "hepkg:method:profile_likelihood", "hepkg:method:pseudo_experiments", "hepkg:method:simultaneous_fit", "hepkg:method:tag_and_probe", "hepkg:method:unbinned_ml_fit"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:1fef1d9b0ad95dbc952f0d79", "hepkg:evidence:8bb0a6550f2b657ec8067355", "hepkg:evidence:b1299d4ef669a0c21896ac2b", "hepkg:evidence:cd4a6f1326af2517b5730ed8", "hepkg:evidence:dbe0118f30bc3399f7bca8e7", "hepkg:evidence:fb1c5173713b138861c30b2c"], "seen_values": ["15", "2", "2401.0709", "2401.07090", "across", "background", "bins", "blinding", "confidence", "data", "data-driven", "density", "efficiency", "estimation", "estimator", "fit", "for", "hepkg:method:data_blinding", "hepkg:method:kde", "hepkg:method:profile_likelihood", "hepkg:method:pseudo_experiments", "hepkg:method:simultaneous_fit", "hepkg:method:tag