{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-7f13bd27", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which statistical methods does analysis 2605.14245 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2605.14245 uses the following statistical methods:\n\n- **CMS Combine statistical analysis tool**\n- **Discrete profiling method for data-driven background modeling** (Note: This is categorized as a background method, but it is included in the results for completeness.)\n- **F-test for optimal function/order selection (signal Gaussian sum and background functions)**\n- **Goodness-of-fit test using the saturated model test statistic**\n- **Likelihood-ratio confidence interval definition under Wilks' theorem violation (-2ΔlnL<1,4)**\n- **Simultaneous extended maximum likelihood fit to diphoton mass spectrum**\n\nThese methods are used to analyze the data and extract meaningful results from the analysis.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2605.14245"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2605.14245"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 6, "error": null, "seconds": 0.037}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:cms_combine_tool", "hepkg:method:discrete_profiling", "hepkg:method:extended_max_likelihood_fit", "hepkg:method:f_test_signal_background", "hepkg:method:saturated_model_gof", "hepkg:method:wilks_theorem_violation_ci"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:0640a6e7ff1b8d0f8974c824", "hepkg:evidence:1742681158db7cf5bb4574c6", "hepkg:evidence:1f6133f616cfb6b2b04149c0", "hepkg:evidence:383af97efe5f0e3df2fef35f", "hepkg:evidence:3a782e4d53616f87e51f3878", "hepkg:evidence:5a962e75c5c82babd762b778", "hepkg:evidence:70afca57a4e765759341e961", "hepkg:evidence:d4694a1e1ff8704f257d78bd", "hepkg:evidence:e02b65bcf36351ea951ecda0"], "seen_values": ["1,4", "14", "2", "2605.14245", "an