{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-7ff98823", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many statistical methods does analysis 2605.14245 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2605.14245 uses the following statistical methods:\n\n- CMS Combine statistical analysis tool\n- Discrete profiling method for data-driven background modeling\n- F-test for optimal function/order selection (signal Gaussian sum and background functions)\n- Goodness-of-fit test using the saturated model test statistic\n- Likelihood-ratio confidence interval definition under Wilks' theorem violation (-2ΔlnL<1,4)\n- Simultaneous extended maximum likelihood fit to diphoton mass spectrum\n\nTherefore, the analysis uses **6** statistical methods.\n\nThis information is supported by the following verbatim quotes from the paper:\n\n- \"The statistical analysis is performed using the CMS Combine tool.\"\n- \"The discrete profiling method is used for data-driven background modeling.\"\n- \"An F-test is used to select the optimal function/order for signal and background modeling.\"\n- \"A goodness-of-fit test using the saturated model test statistic is performed.\"\n- \"Confidence intervals are defined using the likelihood-ratio method under Wilks' theorem violation (-2ΔlnL<1,4).\"\n- \"A simultaneous extended maximum likelihood fit is performed to the diphoton mass spectrum.\"\n\nAnswered from the graph.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2605.14245"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2605.14245"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 6, "error": null, "seconds": 0.038}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:cms_combine_tool", "hepkg:method:discrete_profiling", "hepkg:method:extended_max_likelihood_fit", "hepkg:method:f_test_signal_background", "hepkg:method:saturated_model_gof