{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-83aff6b2", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many statistical methods does analysis 2206.09466 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2206.09466 uses three statistical methods: Binned maximum likelihood fit with log-normal constrained nuisance parameters, LHC Higgs Combination Group statistical approach, and Profile likelihood ratio method. This information is supported by the following verbatim quotes from the paper: - For the binned maximum likelihood fit: \"A binned maximum likelihood fit is performed to the distribution of the discriminant, with the signal and background templates derived from simulation.\" - For the LHC Higgs Combination Group statistical approach: \"The statistical interpretation follows the LHC Higgs Combination Group recommendations.\" - For the profile likelihood ratio method: \"The significance of the observed excess is evaluated using the profile likelihood ratio method.\"", "answered": true, "papers": ["2009.04363", "2206.09466"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2206.09466"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 3, "error": null, "seconds": 0.034}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:binned-maximum-likelihood-fit", "hepkg:method:lhc-higgs-combination-approach", "hepkg:method:profile-likelihood"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:3cec15055cdece69b7fa570a", "hepkg:evidence:5f82c8e2f2c174d7b6bb3ade", "hepkg:evidence:bb2b52bd6031ad50b0b27f86"], "seen_values": ["2206.09466", "approach", "binned", "combination", "constrained", "fit", "group", "hepkg:method:binned-maximum-likelihood-fit", "hepkg:method:lhc-higgs-combination-approach", "hepkg:method:profile-likelihood", "higgs", "lhc", "likelihood", "log-normal", "maximum", "method", "nuisance", "parameters", "profile", "ratio", "result_uses_statistical_method", "statistical", "statistical_method", "with"], "verification_score": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": [], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 7064, "completion_tokens": 388, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 16.02226433204487, "error": ""}, "scores": {"seconds": 16.02226433204487, "llm_calls": 2.0, "tokens": 7452.0, "rounds": 2.0, "errored": 0.0, "answered": 1.0, "abstained": 0.0, "refused_in_text": 0.0, "refusal_flag_disagrees": 0.0, "faithfulness": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": 0.0, "count_correct": 0.0, "tool_calls": 1.0, "tool_errors": 0.0, "tool_error_rate": 0.0, "retrieved_first": 1.0, "entities_retrieved": 3.0, "evidence_quotes": 3.0}}
{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-83b67d9a", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many statistical methods does analysis 2103.06956 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2103.06956 uses 7 statistical methods, including the Asimov dataset for SM expected results, CLs procedure for exclusion limits, discrete profiling method for background m_gg modelling, F-test for determining functional form / parameter order, profile likelihood test statistic, and simultaneous binned maximum likelihood fit to m_gammagamma distributions.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2103.06956", "2109.13808"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2103.06956"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 6, "error": null, "seconds": 0.031}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:background_method:discrete_profiling", "hepkg:statmethod:asimov_dataset", "hepkg:statmethod:binned_ml_fit", "hepkg:statmethod:cls_procedure", "hepkg:statmethod:f_test", "hepkg:statmethod:profile_likelihood_test_statistic"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:81c42ce576b9768794199c50", "hepkg:evidence:b11845bd83bfc8c1b326fd57", "hepkg:evidence:c5c6dc3cbd8201956e1fa63b", "hepkg:evidence:e1b0e040ed727a0cced3965a"], "seen_values": ["2103.06956", "asimov", "background", "background_method", "binned", "cls", "dataset", "determining", "discrete", "distributions", "exclusion", "expected", "f-test", "fit", "for", "form", "functional", "hepkg:background_method:discrete_profiling", "hepkg:statmethod:asimov_dataset", "hepkg:statmethod:binned_ml_fit", "hepkg:statmethod:cls_procedure", "hepkg:statmethod:f_test", "hepkg:statmethod:profile_likelihood_test_statistic", "likelihood", "limits", "m_gammagamma", "m_gg", "maximum", "method", "modelling", "order", "parameter", "procedure", "profile", "profiling", "result_uses_stati