{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-84053332", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many object selection requirements does analysis 2110.11231 define?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2110.11231 defines 22 object selection requirements. Here are some examples:\n\n- \"60 < M(lZ1,lZ2) < 120 GeV\"\n- \"DeepCSV tight working point (~0.1% mistag, 40-60% b-tag efficiency)\"\n- \"M(lZ1,lZ2,lW) > 100 GeV\"\n- \"exactly three tight light leptons with >=1 OSSF pair\"\n- \"pT > 25 GeV, |eta| < 2.5, plus noise-rejection identification criteria\"\n- \"pT > 5 GeV, |eta| < 2.4\"\n- \"pT > 7 GeV, |eta| < 2.5\"\n- \"pT(lZ1) > 25 GeV, pT(lZ2) > 10 GeV, pT(lW) > 25 GeV\"\n- \"p_T^miss > 30 GeV\"\n- \"passes prompt-vs-nonprompt MVA discriminant (tight lepton definition)\"\n\nAnd more. Each of these requirements is part of the selection criteria for the objects used in the analysis.", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2110.11231"], "predicate": "object_has_selection"}, "rows": 23, "error": null, "seconds": 0.035}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": [], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:0a2ef84ce10d9c0c684eae5c", "hepkg:evidence:0e0edb7a129069f686388466", "hepkg:evidence:24cb997b3a0150b8e40243ec", "hepkg:evidence:27f1ecec531b7d154918f1f8", "hepkg:evidence:41c7d17a2e43963661ec5f51", "hepkg:evidence:4d41b83b43306413fa421066", "hepkg:evidence:50eb124d7e9899bad70b1ec0", "hepkg:evidence:5aba00eea241a0d83b01eea3", "hepkg:evidence:5ade233b707952454ea6e7b9", "hepkg:evidence:6910dc1aaec917665134d664", "hepkg:evidence:6a3cdbeca397724ed2b16326", "hepkg:evidence:6b9fa2f24373bf0ae33ba7e0", "hepkg:evidence:71c9e7f10be5c0245a8fd850", "hepkg:evidence:76b963bc5f380cd99cecbe60", "hepkg:evidence:7a2b0b18656f02639819c64e", "hepkg:evidence:90654c8ff7e9279f6f2282f3", "hep