{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-866b3e0b", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2111.08340 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2111.08340 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- $t\\bar{t}$ initial- and final-state radiation modelling uncertainty\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- Jet energy resolution (JER) uncertainty\n- Jet energy scale (JES) uncertainty\n- Jet mass resolution (JMR) uncertainty\n- Jet mass scale (JMS) dominant component uncertainty\n- Jet mass scale (JMS) remaining components uncertainty\n- NLO electroweak correction systematic uncertainty for VBF+VH+ttH\n- Renormalization and factorization scale variation uncertainty for V+jets\n- Single-top-quark (tW, t/s-channel) normalization uncertainty\n- Spurious-signal systematic uncertainty from multijet background modeling\n- VBF, VH, ttH cross-section and acceptance uncertainties\n- W(lnu) cross-section and acceptance uncertainty in CR_ttbar\n- W+jets cross-section uncertainty\n- b-tagging efficiency uncertainty for b-jets\n- b-tagging efficiency uncertainty for c-jets\n- b-tagging efficiency uncertainty for light-flavor jets\n- ggF cross-section and acceptance uncertainty\n- ttbar matrix-element calculation uncertainty (MadGraph5_aMC@NLO vs Powheg Box v2)\n- ttbar parton shower model uncertainty (Herwig7 vs Pythia8)\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the analysis and are relevant to the results presented in the paper.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.03799", "2103.04956", "2106.01676", "2109.13808", "2111.08340", "2202.08676", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2307.01094", "2309.14442", "2401.05299", "2402.08486", "2407.10549", "2