{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-8bc35484", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many background-estimation methods does analysis 2408.03744 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2408.03744 uses the following methods that can be relevant to background estimation:\n\n- Binned maximum likelihood fit for unfolding\n- Data-driven QCD multijet estimation using misidentification factor from isolated/antiisolated control samples\n- Data-driven tag-and-probe method for reconstruction efficiency\n- Simultaneous fit of electron and muon channels assuming lepton flavor universality\n\nThe primary background-estimation method is the **Data-driven QCD multijet estimation using misidentification factor from isolated/antiisolated control samples**.\n\nTherefore, the analysis 2408.03744 uses **one** primary background-estimation method, or **four** methods if all statistical methods relevant to background estimation are considered.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2001.06899", "2112.00895", "2207.12246", "2309.14442", "2401.07090", "2408.03744"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2408.03744"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 5, "error": null, "seconds": 0.037}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:binned_maximum_likelihood_fit", "hepkg:method:combine_tool", "hepkg:method:qcd_misidentification_factor", "hepkg:method:simultaneous_efit_channels", "hepkg:method:tag_and_probe"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:202d4159da8cd9b0f93991ed", "hepkg:evidence:743aff20da5a03d0c93acf74", "hepkg:evidence:7976a0fc9081fabf61cff425", "hepkg:evidence:a27d37fe615c111314a93868", "hepkg:evidence:b7acbd01baa56273700e8815", "hepkg:evidence:cb40892f2d23d7beef6d1f61"], "seen_values": ["2408.03744", "analysis", "and", "antiisolated", "assuming", "background_method", "binned", "channels", "cms", "combine", "control", "data-driven", "efficiency", "electron", "estimation", "factor", "fit", "flavor", "for", "from", "hepkg:method:binned_maximum_likelihood_fit", "hepkg:method:combine_tool", "hepkg:method:qcd_misidentification_factor", "hepkg:method:simultaneous_efit_channels", "hepkg:method:tag_and_probe", "isolated", "lepton", "likelihood", "maximum", "method", "misidentification", "multijet", "muon", "qcd", "reconstruction", "result_uses_statistical_method", "samples", "simultaneous", "statistical", "statistical_method", "tag-and-probe", "tool", "unfolding", "universality", "using"], "verification_score": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": [], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 7211, "completion_tokens": 430, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 17.728952065110207, "error": ""}, "scores": {"seconds": 17.728952065110207, "llm_calls": 2.0, "tokens": 7641.0, "rounds": 2.0, "errored": 0.0, "answered": 1.0, "abstained": 0.0, "refused_in_text": 0.0, "refusal_flag_disagrees": 0.0, "faithfulness": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": 0.0, "count_correct": 0.0, "tool_calls": 1.0, "tool_errors": 0.0, "tool_error_rate": 0.0, "retrieved_first": 1.0, "entities_retrieved": 5.0, "evidence_quotes": 6.0}}
{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-8bf3d0e3", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which simulated samples does analysis 2405.18661 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2405.18661 uses the following simulated samples:\n\n- (POWHEG NLO + MCFM LO)*K_NNLO WW+jets prediction, Pythia8 PS\n- DYTurbo NNLO W/Z prediction (NNPDF3.1), 5 and 13 TeV\n- FEWZ NNLO W/Z prediction (NNPDF2.1), 7 TeV\n- FEWZ NNLO W/Z ratio prediction (MSTW2008), 8 TeV\n- GENEVA NNLO ME + NNLL beam-thrust resummation, Z+jets\n- Higgs ggF signal sample: POWHEG NLO reweighted to NNLO via NNLOPS\n- MadGraph5_aMC LO (<=4 partons) + Pythia8 PS, MLM matching, Z+jets\n- MadGraph5_aMC NLO (<=2 partons) + Pythia8 PS, FxFx matching, Z+jets\n- MadGraph5_aMC@NLO + pythia PS + photos FSR, normalized to FEWZ2.0 NNLO, W charge asymmetry\n- Multi-generator predictions for inelastic pp cross section (pythia6.4/8, phojet, QGSJET-II, sibyll, epos)\n- NLO+NLL jet production prediction at 13 TeV (NLOJet+++fastNLO+NLLJet)\n- NNLOJet NNLO jet production prediction at 13 TeV\n- NNLOJet+fastNLO NNLO QCD jet production prediction (CT18 PDF)\n- NP correction for 13 TeV jet cross section (herwig++ EE5C / pythia8 CP1 average)\n- Nonperturbative correction simulation for fiducial jet cross sections\n- POWHEG v2 + MiNNLO DY simulation for sin2(theta_eff) extraction\n- ttbar signal sample modelled with NLO POWHEG v2 (13 TeV e-mu measurement)\n\nThese samples are used in various parts of the analysis to simulate different processes and backgrounds.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2405.18661"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2405.18661"], "predicate": "result_uses_sample"}, "rows": 17, "error": null, "seconds": 0.042}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:sample:dy_afb_powheg_minnlo", "hepkg:sample:higgs_ggf_signal_powheg_n