{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-8e0ce0c1", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many simulated samples does analysis 2012.03799 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2012.03799 uses 13 simulated samples:\n\n- $V$+jets sample (Sherpa 2.2.1)\n- Alternative W+jets sample generated with MadGraph for generator-modelling systematics\n- Alternative ttbar sample (MadGraph5_aMC@NLO + Pythia 8) for modelling systematics\n- Alternative ttbar sample (Powheg-Box + Herwig 7) for hadronisation systematics\n- Diboson ($VV$) background sample (Sherpa 2.2.1/2.2.2)\n- Multi-leg LO ttbar, Wt and WWbb samples (MadGraph) for ttbar-Wt interference uncertainty\n- Multiboson sample (Sherpa 2.2.1-2.2.2)\n- Nominal $t\\bar{t}$ MC sample (Powheg Box v2+Pythia 8.230)\n- SUSY stop-pair signal sample (MadGraph 2.6.2 + Pythia 8)\n- Single-top s- and Wt-channel sample (Powheg-Box v2 + Pythia 8)\n- Single-top t-channel sample (Powheg-Box v1 + Pythia 8)\n- Spin-0 mediator dark-matter signal sample (MadGraph 2.6.2 + Pythia 8)\n- ttbar+V sample (MG5_aMC@NLO 2.3.3 + Pythia 8)\n\nThis information is based on the content of the paper 2012.03799.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2012.03799 uses 13 simulated samples, including $V$+jets, alternative W+jets, alternative ttbar, diboson, multi-leg LO ttbar, multiboson, nominal $t\\\\bar{t}$, SUSY stop-pair, single-top, spin-0 mediator dark-matter, and ttbar+V samples.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": ["2010.14293", "2012.03799", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2407.10549"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2012.03799"], "predicate": "result_uses_sample"}, "rows": 13, "error": null, "seconds": 0.041}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:sample:dibo