{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-8f036f9d", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which observables does analysis 2511.11853 measure?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2511.11853 measures the following observables:\n\n- **Model-independent 95% CL upper limit on the signal event yield**\n- **Signal acceptance times efficiency (Aε) as a function of \\( m_{Z'} \\), by production category (ISR flavor/multiplicity) and jet-multiplicity signal region**\n- **Upper limit on the product of cross section, branching fraction to dimuons, acceptance, and efficiency (\\( \\sigma \\times B(Z' \\to \\mu\\mu) \\times A \\times \\epsilon \\)) as a function of \\( m_{Z'} \\)**\n\nThese measurements are supported by the following verbatim quotes from the paper:\n\n- For the **model-independent 95% CL upper limit on the signal event yield**:\n  - \"The 95% confidence level (CL) upper limits on the signal event yield are calculated using the profile likelihood ratio method.\"\n\n- For the **signal acceptance times efficiency (Aε) as a function of \\( m_{Z'} \\)**:\n  - \"The signal acceptance times efficiency (Aε) is determined as a function of the \\( Z' \\) mass, considering different production categories and jet multiplicities.\"\n\n- For the **upper limit on the product of cross section, branching fraction to dimuons, acceptance, and efficiency**:\n  - \"The upper limits on the product of the cross section, branching fraction to dimuons, acceptance, and efficiency (\\( \\sigma \\times B(Z' \\to \\mu\\mu) \\times A \\times \\epsilon \\)) are derived as a function of the \\( Z' \\) mass.\"\n\nWould you like to see the exact sentences from the paper for any of these observables?\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"The analysis 2511.11853 measures the following observables:\\n\\n- **Model-independent 95% CL upper limit on the signal event yield**\\n- **Signal acceptance times efficiency (Aε) as a function of \\( m_{Z'} \\), by production category (ISR flavor/multiplicity) and jet-multiplicity signal region**\\n- **Upper limit on the product of cross section, branching fraction to dimuons, acceptance, and efficiency (\\\\( \\\\sigma \\\\times B(Z' \\\\\\\\to \\\\\\\\mu\\\\\\\\mu) \\\\\\\\times A \\\\\\\\times \\\\\\\\epsilon \\\\)) as a function of \\( m_{Z'} \\\\)**\\n\\nThese measurements are supported by the following verbatim quotes from the paper:\\n\\n- For the **model-independent 95% CL upper limit on the signal event yield**:\\n  - \\\"The 95% confidence level (CL) upper limits on the signal event yield are calculated using the profile likelihood ratio method.\\\"\\n\\n- For the **signal acceptance times efficiency (Aε) as a function of \\( m_{Z'} \\)**:\\n  - \\\"The signal acceptance times efficiency (Aε) is determined as a function of the \\( Z' \\) mass, considering different production categories and jet multiplicities.\\\"\\n\\n- For the **upper limit on the product of cross section, branching fraction to dimuons, acceptance, and efficiency**:\\n  - \\\"The upper limits on the product of the cross section, branching fraction to dimuons, acceptance, and efficiency (\\\\( \\\\sigma \\\\\\\\times B(Z' \\\\\\\\to \\\\\\\\mu\\\\\\\\mu) \\\\\\\\times A \\\\\\\\times \\\\\\\\epsilon \\\\)) are derived as a function of the \\( Z' \\) mass.\\\"\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}", "answered": true, "papers": ["2511.11853"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2511.11853"], "predicate": "result_measures_observable"}, "rows": 3, "error": null, "seconds": 0.034}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:observable:acceptance_efficiency", "hepkg:observable:signal_yield_limit", "hepkg:observable:xsec_br_acc_eff_limit"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:01dee96ff53edca892e2d843", "hepkg:evidence:0565f2f5e