{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-8f23b4bd", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which simulated samples does analysis 2208.12095 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2208.12095 uses the following simulated samples:\n\n- $V{+}\\text{jets}$ ($W$ or $Z$ boson) MC sample (Sherpa 2.2.1)\n- $tWZ$ and $tZ$ MC sample (MadGraph5_aMC@NLO 2.3.3 + Pythia 8.212)\n- $t\\bar{t}H$ MC sample (Powheg Box v2 + Pythia 8.230)\n- $t\\bar{t}V$ MC sample (MadGraph5_aMC@NLO 2.3.3 + Pythia 8.210)\n- Alternative $t\\bar{t}$ PS/hadronisation sample (Powheg Box v2 + Herwig 7.04)\n- Alternative single-top PS/hadronisation sample (Powheg Box v2 + Herwig 7.04)\n- Diboson ($WW$, $ZZ$, $WZ$) MC sample (Sherpa 2.2.1/2.2.2)\n- Nominal $t\\bar{t}$ signal MC sample (Powheg Box v2 + Pythia 8.230)\n- Protos MC sample with heavy axigluon (CTEQ6L1 PDF)\n- Single-top $s$-channel MC sample (Powheg Box v2)\n- Single-top $t$-channel MC sample (Powheg Box v2)\n- Single-top $tW$ MC sample (Powheg Box v2, DR scheme)\n\nThese samples are used to simulate various processes and backgrounds in the analysis.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2001.06899", "2208.12095", "2302.05225"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2208.12095"], "predicate": "result_uses_sample"}, "rows": 12, "error": null, "seconds": 0.04}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:benchmark:protos_axigluon", "hepkg:sample:diboson_sherpa", "hepkg:sample:single_top_herwig7_alt", "hepkg:sample:single_top_s_channel_powheg", "hepkg:sample:single_top_t_channel_powheg", "hepkg:sample:single_top_tw_powheg", "hepkg:sample:tWZ_tZ_madgraph", "hepkg:sample:ttH_powheg", "hepkg:sample:ttV_madgraph", "hepkg:sample:ttbar_powheg_herwig7", "hepkg:sample:ttbar_powheg_pythia8", "hepkg:sample:v_jets_sherpa221"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:12682b31c0235a458301e