{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-9393cd1f", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which background-estimation methods does analysis 2408.03744 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2408.03744 uses the following background-estimation methods:\n\n- Binned maximum likelihood fit for unfolding\n- Data-driven QCD multijet estimation using misidentification factor from isolated/antiisolated control samples\n- Data-driven tag-and-probe method for reconstruction efficiency\n- Simultaneous fit of electron and muon channels assuming lepton flavor universality\n\nThese methods are part of the statistical techniques employed in the analysis. The evidence for these methods is directly from the paper.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2001.06899", "2112.00895", "2207.12246", "2309.14442", "2401.07090", "2408.03744"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2408.03744"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 5, "error": null, "seconds": 0.037}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:binned_maximum_likelihood_fit", "hepkg:method:combine_tool", "hepkg:method:qcd_misidentification_factor", "hepkg:method:simultaneous_efit_channels", "hepkg:method:tag_and_probe"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:202d4159da8cd9b0f93991ed", "hepkg:evidence:743aff20da5a03d0c93acf74", "hepkg:evidence:7976a0fc9081fabf61cff425", "hepkg:evidence:a27d37fe615c111314a93868", "hepkg:evidence:b7acbd01baa56273700e8815", "hepkg:evidence:cb40892f2d23d7beef6d1f61"], "seen_values": ["2408.03744", "analysis", "and", "antiisolated", "assuming", "background_method", "binned", "channels", "cms", "combine", "control", "data-driven", "efficiency", "electron", "estimation", "factor", "fit", "flavor", "for", "from", "hepkg:method:binned_maximum_likelihood_fit", "hepkg:method:combine_tool", "hepkg:method:qcd_m