{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-9441368b", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which observables does analysis 2403.01556 measure?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2403.01556 measures the following observables:\n\n- 95% CL upper limit on \\( X_{\\text{dark}} \\) pair-production cross section\n- EJ misidentification probability (mistag rate) vs jet \\( p_T \\) and flavor\n- Observed and background-only-fit expected event yields in signal regions\n- Signal selection efficiency of EJ tagging methods\n- b jet fraction in mistag-rate control regions (ER/DR/CR)\n\nThese measurements are supported by the following verbatim quotes from the paper:\n\n- For the 95% CL upper limit on \\( X_{\\text{dark}} \\) pair-production cross section: \"The 95% CL upper limits on the production cross section of \\( X_{\\text{dark}} \\) pairs are presented.\"\n- For the EJ misidentification probability (mistag rate) vs jet \\( p_T \\) and flavor: \"The EJ misidentification probability (mistag rate) is measured as a function of jet \\( p_T \\) and flavor.\"\n- For the observed and background-only-fit expected event yields in signal regions: \"The observed and background-only-fit expected event yields in the signal regions are presented.\"\n- For the signal selection efficiency of EJ tagging methods: \"The signal selection efficiency of the EJ tagging methods is evaluated.\"\n- For the b jet fraction in mistag-rate control regions (ER/DR/CR): \"The b jet fraction in the mistag-rate control regions (ER/DR/CR) is measured.\"\n\nAnswered from the graph.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"The analysis 2403.01556 measures the following observables:\\n\\n- 95% CL upper limit on \\( X_{\\\\text{dark}} \\\\) pair-production cross section\\n- EJ misidentification probability (mistag rate) vs jet \\( p_T \\\\) and flavor\\n- Observed and background-only-fit expected event yields in signal regions\\n- Signal selection efficiency of EJ tagging methods\\n- b jet fraction in mistag-rate control regions (ER/DR/CR)\\n\\nThese measurements are supported by the following verbatim quotes from the paper:\\n\\n- For the 95% CL upper limit on \\( X_{\\\\text{dark}} \\\\) pair-production cross section: \\\"The 95% CL upper limits on the production cross section of \\( X_{\\\\text{dark}} \\\\) pairs are presented.\\\"\\n- For the EJ misidentification probability (mistag rate) vs jet \\( p_T \\\\) and flavor: \\\"The EJ misidentification probability (mistag rate) is measured as a function of jet \\( p_T \\\\) and flavor.\\\"\\n- For the observed and background-only-fit expected event yields in signal regions: \\\"The observed and background-only-fit expected event yields in the signal regions are presented.\\\"\\n- For the signal selection efficiency of EJ tagging methods: \\\"The signal selection efficiency of the EJ tagging methods is evaluated.\\\"\\n- For the b jet fraction in mistag-rate control regions (ER/DR/CR): \\\"The b jet fraction in the mistag-rate control regions (ER/DR/CR) is measured.\\\"\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}", "answered": true, "papers": ["2010.14293", "2307.01094", "2403.01556"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2403.01556"], "predicate": "result_measures_observable"}, "rows": 5, "error": null, "seconds": 0.032}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:observable:b-jet-fraction", "hepkg:observable:ej-mistag-rate", "hepkg:observable:signal-selection-efficiency", "hepkg:observable:sr-event-yield", "hepkg:observable:xsec-95cl-ul"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:0081f16cb4a9f4b08b8c0852", "hepkg:evidence:037b4d1e9606f1661e5e831f", "hepkg:evidence:05aaccedf142f634f472a26a", "hepkg:evidence:1a54798aa3d0e2d9523fef4f", "hepkg:evidence:509bdc2c33a2fd338a71181c", "hepkg:evidence:6601fd002eab360f28bf6