{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-9cad3376", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2011.07812 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2011.07812 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- High-|d0| tracking efficiency uncertainty from comparison of signal MC and cosmic-tagged muon data\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- SUSY signal cross-section theoretical uncertainty (PDF4LHC15_mc, approximate NNLO+NNLL)\n- Statistical uncertainty on lepton trigger/reconstruction/selection efficiency scale factors (from Z boson decays)\n- Uncertainty from filtering selection used for extended (large-radius) track reconstruction\n- Uncertainty from impact of pileup on signal selection\n- Uncertainty from varying factorization and renormalization scales in signal cross section prediction\n- Uncertainty from |d0| dependence of lepton reconstruction and selection efficiency vs. tracking efficiency in simulation\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the paper with the arXiv ID 2011.07812.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.03799", "2103.04956", "2106.01676", "2109.13808", "2111.08340", "2202.08676", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2307.01094", "2401.05299", "2402.08486", "2407.10549", "2503.19420", "2506.13565", "2510.07527", "2604.21670"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2011.07812"], "predicate": "result_has_systematic"}, "rows": 8, "error": null, "seconds": 0.046}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:systematic:d0-dependence-selection-efficiency", "hepkg:systematic:extended-track-filtering", "hepkg:systematic:factorization-renormalization-scale", "hepkg:systematic:high-d0-t