{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-a1d66dc7", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2408.03744 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2408.03744 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- ECAL L1 trigger prefiring correction uncertainty\n- EW + ttbar background cross section / normalization uncertainty\n- Finite simulated sample size statistical uncertainty\n- Hadronic recoil calibration uncertainty\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- Lepton momentum scale and resolution modeling uncertainty\n- Lepton reconstruction/identification/trigger efficiency statistical uncertainty\n- Lepton reconstruction/identification/trigger efficiency systematic uncertainty (tag-and-probe modeling)\n- PDF and strong coupling alpha_S uncertainty in kinematic acceptance\n- QCD multijet background estimation statistical uncertainty (misidentification factor)\n- QCD multijet background estimation systematic uncertainty\n- Renormalization and factorization scale (muR, muF) uncertainty in kinematic acceptance\n- Resummation (DYturbo vs MadGraph5_aMC@NLO) and FSR modeling uncertainty in kinematic acceptance\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the analysis.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2012.01581", "2103.06956", "2109.13808", "2112.00895", "2112.03161", "2309.14442", "2408.03744", "2509.22535"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2408.03744"], "predicate": "result_has_systematic"}, "rows": 13, "error": null, "seconds": 0.047}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:systematic:efficiency_stat", "hepkg:systematic:efficiency_syst", "hepkg:systematic:ew_ttbar_cross_section", "hepkg:systematic:hadronic_recoil_calibration", "hepkg:systematic:integrated_luminosity", "hepkg:systematic:lepton_momentum_scale_resolution", "hepkg:systemati