{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-a2c951a0", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which background-estimation methods does analysis 2111.08340 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2111.08340 uses the following background-estimation methods:\n\n- Beeston-Barlow \"lite\" technique for limited MC sample-size statistical uncertainties\n- Binned maximum-likelihood (global likelihood) fit using RooStats\n- CLs method for upper limit derivation\n- Log-likelihood ratio (LLR) test based on Wilks' theorem\n\nThese methods are used for various aspects of the statistical analysis, including handling limited Monte Carlo sample sizes, fitting the data, setting upper limits, and performing hypothesis tests.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2111.08340", "2312.04450", "2401.05299"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2111.08340"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 4, "error": null, "seconds": 0.035}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:beeston-barlow-lite", "hepkg:method:cls-limit", "hepkg:method:global-likelihood-fit", "hepkg:method:llr-wilks-test"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:0644b290e931ba2c64ed5eaf", "hepkg:evidence:278b026616ea9f43ee61d338", "hepkg:evidence:5031ae4fd39bdc3018dce6f1", "hepkg:evidence:54d2db6f0472fea704474779", "hepkg:evidence:8f5210bd195d0bb5652f6a27"], "seen_values": ["2111.0834", "2111.08340", "based", "beeston-barlow", "binned", "cls", "derivation", "fit", "for", "global", "hepkg:method:beeston-barlow-lite", "hepkg:method:cls-limit", "hepkg:method:global-likelihood-fit", "hepkg:method:llr-wilks-test", "likelihood", "limit", "limited", "lite", "llr", "log-likelihood", "maximum-likelihood", "method", "ratio", "result_uses_statistical_method", "roostats", "sample-size", "statistical", "statistical_method", "technique", "test"