{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-a4bcaaee", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which statistical methods does analysis 2504.13081 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2504.13081 uses the following statistical methods:\n\n- **Combination of binned (template-based) and unbinned (parametric) likelihoods across analyses**\n- **Fit to the Asimov data set to obtain expected covariance matrix**\n- **Likelihood ratio test statistic \\( q(\\mu) \\) for confidence intervals**\n- **Principal component analysis of the Fisher information matrix to identify constrained linear combinations of Wilson coefficients**\n- **Profiling of nuisance parameters in the maximum likelihood fit**\n- **Simultaneous extended maximum likelihood fit across analysis categories**\n- **Wilks' theorem used to obtain two-dimensional confidence contours**\n\nThese methods are recorded in the graph based on the content of the paper.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2403.01556", "2504.13081"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2504.13081"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 7, "error": null, "seconds": 0.036}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:statmethod:asimov-dataset-fit", "hepkg:statmethod:binned-unbinned-likelihood-combination", "hepkg:statmethod:likelihood-ratio-test-statistic", "hepkg:statmethod:pca-fisher-info", "hepkg:statmethod:profiled-nuisance-parameters", "hepkg:statmethod:simultaneous-extended-ml-fit", "hepkg:statmethod:wilks-theorem"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:03e13319bbd9572f9e1625ae", "hepkg:evidence:04776c72104d27a867f9c59a", "hepkg:evidence:2260ec7d800134788c4fbe00", "hepkg:evidence:311d461a48e8d953f648a6ed", "hepkg:evidence:3783c1337432fae455d573c9", "hepkg:evidence:472ef4fee1820e4050c038ee", "hepkg:evidence:7881fae2ec74a5a5f7704f7b"], "seen_va