{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-a6aa7d1a", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2112.00895 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2112.00895 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- Charge-symmetric ttbar dilepton background residual after OS-SS subtraction\n- Charm fragmentation function (energy-fraction) modelling uncertainty\n- Charm quark fragmentation fractions uncertainty\n- Charm semileptonic branching fraction \\( B(c \\to l) \\) uncertainty (SL channel)\n- D0/D+ decay branching fraction correction uncertainty (SV channel)\n- Gluon splitting rate into \\( c \\bar{c} \\) uncertainty\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- Jet energy scale and resolution uncertainty\n- Lepton charge misidentification uncertainty\n- Lepton trigger, reconstruction and identification efficiency uncertainty\n- Limited size of simulated (MC) samples uncertainty\n- Missing transverse momentum (MET) resolution/mismeasurement uncertainty\n- Muon-inside-jet identification efficiency uncertainty (SL channel)\n- PDF modelling uncertainty (CT14, MMHT2014 vs NNPDF3.0 replicas)\n- Pile-up modelling uncertainty\n- Secondary vertex charge assignment uncertainty\n- Secondary vertex reconstruction efficiency scale-factor uncertainty\n- Semileptonic ttbar background modelling uncertainty (real OS events)\n- Single top quark background normalization uncertainty\n- W+udsg light-flavour jet mismodelling uncertainty\n- Z+jets background modelling uncertainty (Z mass peak region)\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the analysis.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2007.02873", "2012.01581", "2103.06956", "2109.13808", "2112.00895", "2112.03161", "2208.12095", "2303.15340", "2309.14442", "2408.03744", "2509.22535", "2510.07527", "2602.18611", "2604.21670", "2605.14245"], "value": null