{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-ae29300d", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many object selection requirements does analysis 2506.13565 define?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2506.13565 defines 22 object selection requirements. Here are some examples:\n\n- **\"1.44 < |η_C| < 1.57 rejected (ECAL transition region)\"**\n- **\"1.57 < |η_C| < 2.50 (ECAL endcap region)\"**\n- **\"DeepJet relaxed working point applied to other b jets; typical efficiency 68%, misid light/gluon 1.0%, misid c 12%\"**\n- **\"DeepJet tight working point applied to highest-pT b jet; efficiency ~50%, misid light/gluon 0.1%, misid c 2.4%\"**\n- **\"HLT: two electrons with pT > 33 (25) GeV in 2016/2017 (2018)\"**\n- **\"L1: single muon pT > 22 GeV; HLT: pT > 50 GeV (additional pT>100 GeV triggers in 2017-2018)\"**\n- **\"TuneP algorithm used for pT > 200 GeV muons\"**\n- **\"angle between two muons < π - 0.02 (cosmic ray suppression)\"**\n- **\"anti-kT clustering, distance parameter 0.4, from PF candidates\"**\n- **\"isolation: scalar sum pT of tracks in cone dR<0.3 does not exceed 5% of muon pT\"**\n- **\"loose veto electron: pT > 10 GeV, |η| < 2.5\"**\n- **\"loose veto muon: pT > 10 GeV, |η| < 2.4\"**\n- **\"opposite electric charge required for muon pair\"**\n- **\"pT > 20 GeV\"**\n- **\"pT > 35 GeV\"**\n- **\"pT > 53 GeV\"**\n- **\"p_T^miss = negative vector pT sum of all PF candidates\"**\n- **\"|d_xy| < 0.02 cm (barrel); |d_xy| < 0.05 cm (endcap), relative to primary vertex\"**\n- **\"|d_z| < 0.1 cm and |d_xy| < 0.02 cm relative to primary vertex\"**\n- **\"|η_C| < 1.44 (ECAL barrel region)\"**\n- **\"|η| < 2.4 accepted\"**\n- **\"|η| < 2.4\"**\n\nThese selections are detailed in the paper and are used to define the criteria for various detector objects. \n\nAnswered from the graph.", "answered": true, "papers": [], "