{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-ae4338c9", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many object selection requirements does analysis 2201.11585 define?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2201.11585 defines 18 object selection requirements. Here are some examples:\n\n- \\(160 \\, \\text{GeV} < p_T^\\text{miss} < 250 \\, \\text{GeV} \\, (\\text{VTR SR})\\)\n- \\(p_T > 10 \\, \\text{GeV}\\)\n- \\(p_T > 20 \\, \\text{GeV}\\)\n- \\(p_T > 230 \\, \\text{GeV} \\, (\\text{tight})\\)\n- \\(p_T > 30 \\, \\text{GeV}, |\\eta| < 4.7\\)\n- \\(p_T^\\text{miss} > 250 \\, \\text{GeV} \\, (\\text{MTR SR})\\)\n- \\(| \\eta | < 2.4\\)\n- \\(| \\eta | > 2.99, p_T > 80 \\, \\text{GeV} \\, (\\text{event veto if fails shower-shape criteria})\\)\n\nThese selections are crucial for defining the kinematic and quality criteria for the objects used in the analysis.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2201.11585 defines 18 object selection requirements. Examples include: \\(160 \\\\, \\\\text{GeV} < p_T^\\\\text{miss} < 250 \\\\, \\\\text{GeV} \\\\, (\\\\text{VTR SR})\\), \\(p_T > 10 \\\\, \\\\text{GeV}\\), \\(p_T > 20 \\\\, \\\\text{GeV}\\), \\(p_T > 230 \\\\, \\\\text{GeV} \\\\, (\\\\text{tight})\\), \\(p_T > 30 \\\\, \\\\text{GeV}, |\\\\eta| < 4.7\\), \\(p_T^\\\\text{miss} > 250 \\\\, \\\\text{GeV} \\\\, (\\\\text{MTR SR})\\), \\(| \\\\eta | < 2.4\\), and \\(| \\\\eta | > 2.99, p_T > 80 \\\\, \\\\text{GeV} \\\\, (\\\\text{event veto if fails shower-shape criteria})\\).\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2201.11585"], "predicate": "object_has_selection"}, "rows": 18, "error": null, "seconds": 0.04}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": [], "evidence_ids": ["he