{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-af161d13", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2010.14293 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2010.14293 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- Control-region data statistical uncertainty (CR sample size)\n- Diboson ($WZ$/$ZZ$+jets) modelling uncertainty\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- Jet energy scale (JES), jet energy resolution (JER) and \\(E_T^\\text{miss}\\) soft-term uncertainty\n- Lepton reconstruction and b-tag/b-veto efficiency uncertainty (found negligible)\n- MC background sample statistical (limited-event) uncertainty\n- Multi-jet background estimate uncertainty (uniform 100%)\n- Pile-up reweighting uncertainty (found negligible)\n- SUSY signal ISR/FSR modelling uncertainty (generator tune and scale variation, function of mass splitting)\n- SUSY signal cross-section uncertainty (renormalisation/factorisation scale, PDF, \\(\\alpha_s\\) variation)\n- Statistical uncertainty in \\(\\gamma\\)+jets-to-\\(Z\\)+jets kappa correction factor\n- Theoretical modelling uncertainty from generator comparison and renormalisation/factorisation scale variation\n- W/Z+jets modelling uncertainty (CKKW-L merging/resummation scale, PDF, \\(\\alpha_s\\), ME scale variations)\n- \\(t\\bar{t}\\) background modelling uncertainty (parton shower/hadronisation, generator choice, ISR/FSR, scale variations)\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the analysis 2010.14293.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2012.03799", "2103.04956", "2106.01676", "2109.13808", "2111.08340", "2202.08676", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2307.01094", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2402.08486", "2403.01556",