{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-b2315ff1", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which simulated samples does analysis 2605.14245 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2605.14245 uses the following simulated samples:\n\n- Drell-Yan (DY) sample (MadGraph5_aMC@NLO)\n- SM diphoton background sample (SHERPA v2.2.4)\n- SM ggH, VBF and ttH signal samples (MadGraph5_aMC@NLO NLO) - HVV analysis\n- VBF Higgs samples generated with POWHEG for multivariate discriminant training\n- VBF and VH SM and anomalous-coupling samples (JHUGen LO) - HVV analysis\n- VBF and ttH resonant-background samples (MadGraph5_aMC@NLO) - ggH analysis\n- VBF, ZH and WH SM and BSM samples (JHUGen LO QCD) - ggH analysis\n- WH and ZH signal samples (POWHEG 2.0 NLO) - HVV analysis\n- WH resonant-background sample (JHUGen) - ggH analysis\n- ZH resonant-background sample (POWHEG) - ggH analysis\n- gamma+jet and jet+jet background sample (PYTHIA 8, LO)\n- ggH+2 jets SM and anomalous-coupling samples (POWHEG+MiNLO NLO) - ggH analysis\n- ggH+2 jets comparison samples (JHUGen, and MadGraph5_aMC@NLO/POWHEG for SM contributions)\n\nThese samples are used in various parts of the analysis to simulate different processes and backgrounds.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2605.14245"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2605.14245"], "predicate": "result_uses_sample"}, "rows": 13, "error": null, "seconds": 0.045}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:sample:diphoton_sherpa", "hepkg:sample:drell_yan_mg5amcnlo", "hepkg:sample:gamma_jet_jetjet_pythia", "hepkg:sample:ggh_2jets_jhugen_comparison", "hepkg:sample:ggh_2jets_signal_powheg_minlo", "hepkg:sample:ggh_vbf_tth_signal_mg5amcnlo", "hepkg:sample:vbf_powheg_training", "hepkg:sample:vbf_tth_mg5amcnlo_gganalysis", "hepkg:sample:vbf_vh_anomalous_jhugen", "hepkg:sa