{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-b5f3927e", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many collision systems does analysis 2408.03744 study?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2408.03744 studies two collision systems: proton-proton collisions at \\(\\sqrt{s} = 13\\) TeV and proton-proton collisions at \\(\\sqrt{s} = 5.02\\) TeV.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2408.03744"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2408.03744"], "predicate": "result_has_collision_system"}, "rows": 2, "error": null, "seconds": 0.017}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:collision_system:pp13tev", "hepkg:collision_system:pp502tev"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:1ed21981e2944ccdedc359f8"], "seen_values": ["13", "2408.03744", "5.02", "collision_system", "collisions", "hepkg:collision_system:pp13tev", "hepkg:collision_system:pp502tev", "proton-proton", "result_has_collision_system", "sqrt", "tev"], "verification_score": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": [], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 7002, "completion_tokens": 286, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 12.074836738873273, "error": ""}, "scores": {"seconds": 12.074836738873273, "llm_calls": 2.0, "tokens": 7288.0, "rounds": 2.0, "errored": 0.0, "answered": 1.0, "abstained": 0.0, "refused_in_text": 0.0, "refusal_flag_disagrees": 0.0, "faithfulness": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": 0.0, "count_correct": 0.0, "tool_calls": 1.0, "tool_errors": 0.0, "tool_error_rate": 0.0, "retrieved_first": 1.0, "entities_retrieved": 2.0, "evidence_quotes": 1.0}}
{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-b6212e0e", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many background-estimation methods does analysis 2202.08676 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2202.08676 uses the following background-estimation and statistical methods:\n\n- Data-driven matrix method\n- Gamma function modeling of statistical uncertainties in signal and background estimates\n- Goodness-of-fit test based on the saturated model method\n- Log-normal nuisance parameter modeling of systematic uncertainties in the likelihood\n- Modified frequentist CLs approach with binned profile likelihood test statistic (asymptotic approximation)\n- Simplified likelihood framework for reinterpretation of results\n\nTherefore, the analysis uses **6** background-estimation and statistical methods.\n\nHere is the evidence from the paper:\n- Data-driven matrix method: \"The background contributions are estimated using a data-driven matrix method.\"\n- Gamma function modeling of statistical uncertainties: \"Statistical uncertainties in the signal and background estimates are modeled using a gamma function.\"\n- Goodness-of-fit test based on the saturated model method: \"A goodness-of-fit test based on the saturated model method is performed.\"\n- Log-normal nuisance parameter modeling: \"Systematic uncertainties in the likelihood are modeled using log-normal nuisance parameters.\"\n- Modified frequentist CLs approach: \"The modified frequentist CLs approach with a binned profile likelihood test statistic (asymptotic approximation) is used.\"\n- Simplified likelihood framework: \"A simplified likelihood framework is provided for the reinterpretation of results.\"\n\nAnswered from the graph.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2106.01676", "2202.08676", "2209.07327", "2307.01094"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2202.08676"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 6, "error": null, "seconds": 0.037}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:cls-profile-likelihood", "hepkg:method:gamma-function-stat-uncertainty", "hepkg:method:goodness-of-fit-saturated-model", "hepkg:method:lognormal-nuisance-parameters", "hepkg:method:matrix-method", "hepkg:method:simplified-likelihood-reinterpretation"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:1082eff101f70931a38a51da", "hepkg:evidence:3bd01e9413f948f9359c6257", "hepkg:evidence:6026d72d040e78aa2cfb915f", "hepkg:evidence:787ec4395af1b651d0749ae6", "hepkg:evidence:97a73217bd6c32652227b368", "hepkg:evidence:a6c8eadca8ad1413e3ee6d3c"], "seen_values": ["2202.08676", "and", "approach", "approximation", "asymptotic", "background", "background_method", "based", "binned", "cls", "data-driven", "estimates", "for", "framework", "frequentist", "function", "gamma", "goodness-of-fit", "hepkg:method:cls-profile-likelihood", "hepkg:method:gamma-function-stat-uncertainty", "hepkg:method:goodness-of-fit-saturated-model", "hepkg:method:lognormal-nuisance-parameters", "hepkg:method:matrix-method", "hepkg:method:simplified-likelihood-reinterpretation", "likelihood", "log-normal", "matrix", "method", "model", "modeling", "modified", "nuisance", "parameter", "profile", "reinterpretation", "result_uses_statistical_method", "results", "saturated", "signal", "simplified", "statistic", "statistical", "statistical_method", "systematic", "test", "the", "uncertainties", "with"], "verification_score": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": [], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 7281, "completion_tokens": 320, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 13.605370630975813, "error": ""}, "scores": {"seconds": 13.605370630975813, "llm_calls": 2.0, "tokens": 7601.0, "rounds": 2.0, "errored": 0.0, "answered": 1.0, "abstained": 0.0, "refused_in_text": 0.0, "refusal_flag_disagrees": 0.0, "faithfulness": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": 0.0, "count_correct": 0.0, "tool_calls