{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-b660efd9", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which background-estimation methods does analysis 2304.08962 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2304.08962 uses the following background-estimation methods:\n\n- Asymptotic profile-likelihood-ratio formula \\( Z = \\sqrt{2 \\ln \\left[\\frac{L(s_{\\text{hat}}, \\theta_{\\text{hat}})}{L(0, \\theta_{\\text{hat\\_hat}})}\\right]} \\) for significance calculation.\n- Simultaneous signal-region/control-region likelihood with nuisance parameters constrained by Gaussian subsidiary measurements.\n- Toy Monte Carlo studies used to exclude alternative fit models (two-resonance interfering / three-resonance non-interfering) at >95% CL relative to model A.\n- Unbinned maximum likelihood fit to the 4mu invariant mass spectra.\n\nThese methods are detailed in the paper and are used to estimate and validate the background in the analysis.", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2304.08962"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 4, "error": null, "seconds": 0.037}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": [], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:05a9ee2bdc4b926c32444d96", "hepkg:evidence:24f72e1f323cf0e953defcd2", "hepkg:evidence:8b7ebd7a0284234ce781c0b7", "hepkg:evidence:90de6b8d32de1d36c1fdab5c"], "seen_values": ["0", "2", "2304.08962", "4", "95", "alternative", "asymptotic", "calculation", "carlo", "constrained", "control-region", "exclude", "fit", "for", "formula", "gaussian", "interfering", "invariant", "likelihood", "mass", "maximum", "measurements", "model", "models", "monte", "non-interfering", "none", "nuisance", "parameters", "profile-likelihood-ratio", "relative", "result_uses_statistical_method", "s_hat", "signal-region", "significance", "simultaneous", 