{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-b8725ba0", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many background-estimation methods does analysis 2102.01444 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2102.01444 uses seven statistical methods for background estimation:\n\n1. CLs method for deriving exclusion confidence levels\n2. Fit performed with standard minimisation software, floating background normalisations with MC-derived shapes\n3. Likelihood constructed as product of Poisson pdfs (observed yields per CR/SR) and Gaussian pdfs for nuisance parameters\n4. Model-independent hypothesis test introducing a free signal strength constrained by observed SR yield\n5. Pseudo-experiments used to compute expected/observed limits and discovery p-values\n6. Simultaneous likelihood fit using HistFitter and pyhf minimisation packages\n7. Simultaneous profile likelihood fit in dedicated background control regions\n\nThese methods are recorded in the graph as used by this analysis.", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2102.01444"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 7, "error": null, "seconds": 0.037}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": [], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:071a0012f7b999dffe712de7", "hepkg:evidence:086b8f62840c2b2899756603", "hepkg:evidence:41e414d43e32578bac7ff1b7", "hepkg:evidence:615643a033a20f0c7a65843f", "hepkg:evidence:b3e803d54c7f33a5b9590b9f", "hepkg:evidence:c6463fc73dd197dd2881bc7f", "hepkg:evidence:d915d341ab851e7c778ef15e", "hepkg:evidence:e7ee9948dc4cb0152b634b94"], "seen_values": ["2102.01444", "and", "background", "cls", "compute", "confidence", "constrained", "constructed", "control", "dedicated", "deriving", "discovery", "exclusion", "expected", "fit", "floating", "for", "free", "gaussian", "histfitter", "hypo