{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-c14e1290", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2312.04450 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2312.04450 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- $Z$+jets modelling uncertainty\n- $tWZ$ modelling uncertainty (DR1 vs DR2 diagram removal)\n- $tZq$ modelling uncertainty\n- $t\\bar{t}Z$ A14 tune (ISR, Var3c) uncertainty\n- $t\\bar{t}Z$ parton-shower/underlying-event modelling uncertainty\n- $t\\bar{t}Z$ renormalisation/factorisation scale ($\\mu_f$, $\\mu_r$) uncertainty\n- Background normalisation uncertainties (combined inclusive fit)\n- Data-driven $t\\bar{t}$ background estimation uncertainty\n- Diboson ($WZ$/$ZZ$+jets) modelling uncertainty\n- Fake/non-prompt lepton background uncertainty\n- Flavour-tagging (b-tagging) uncertainty\n- Integrated luminosity measurement uncertainty\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty (propagated impact on cross section)\n- Jets and missing transverse momentum uncertainties\n- Lepton reconstruction/identification/isolation/scale/resolution uncertainty\n- MC background sample statistical (limited-event) uncertainty\n- Other (minor) background normalisation uncertainty\n- PDF uncertainty (signal and backgrounds, PDF4LHC prescription)\n- Pile-up reweighting uncertainty\n- Total systematic uncertainty on the combined inclusive $t\\bar{t}Z$ cross section\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the analysis 2312.04450.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2006.05880", "2010.14293", "2106.01676", "2211.08028", "2312.04450"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2312.04450"], "predicate": "result_has_systematic"}, "rows": 20, "error": null, "seconds": 0.05}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:systematic:b-tagging", "hepkg:systematic:background-