{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-c5344d77", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which background-estimation methods does analysis 2604.21670 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2604.21670 uses the following background-estimation methods:\n\n- Asimov-data expected limit estimation\n- Bootstrap-based statistical correlation tests\n- Multivariate Gaussian likelihood model\n- Poisson likelihood with Gaussian-constrained nuisance parameters\n- Principal Component Analysis for fit-basis direction identification\n- Profile likelihood ratio test statistic\n- Simplified likelihood model from measurement covariance matrix\n- Toy (pseudo-experiment) based confidence interval construction\n- Wilks' theorem for confidence-interval estimation\n\nThese methods are recorded in the graph as being used in this analysis.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2201.11585", "2309.14442", "2604.21670"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2604.21670"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 9, "error": null, "seconds": 0.036}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:asimov_data", "hepkg:method:bootstrap_correlation_test", "hepkg:method:multivariate_gaussian_likelihood", "hepkg:method:pca_fit_basis", "hepkg:method:poisson_likelihood", "hepkg:method:profile_likelihood_ratio", "hepkg:method:simplified_likelihood_model", "hepkg:method:toy_based_confidence_intervals", "hepkg:method:wilks_theorem"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:03a3038883958c1e8ff5041a", "hepkg:evidence:29c1a504d67c60ad4aa00ec8", "hepkg:evidence:467e5d3f010b4a46f763a1f2", "hepkg:evidence:46bc0d208a8ea6815f0cccf3", "hepkg:evidence:5db848734bfff51acd0a5bbc", "hepkg:evidence:81d1bb3f8b4d8993e51d224a", "hepkg:evidence:8ace8bcc113c9a9c5a29ab76", "hepkg:evidence:c95ccbdbf418c6a2529aa5a4", "hepkg:evidence:edc7a5