{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-c9336aec", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many background-estimation methods does analysis 2006.05880 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2006.05880 uses 7 statistical methods for background estimation:\n\n1. Background-only fit (CRs only, no signal, floating WZ normalisation)\n2. CLs prescription for 95% CL exclusion limits\n3. HistFitter package with Gaussian nuisance parameters for systematic uncertainties\n4. Maximum-likelihood (profile likelihood) fit with Poisson/Gaussian terms and Beeston-Barlow-lite MC-stat nuisances\n5. Poisson statistical modelling with Gaussian-constrained nuisance parameters\n6. Pseudo-experiment-based calculation of limits and discovery p-values\n7. Shape-fit approach using mutually exclusive kinematic bins\n\nThese methods are documented in the paper.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2006.05880 uses 7 statistical methods for background estimation:\\n\\n1. Background-only fit (CRs only, no signal, floating WZ normalisation)\\n2. CLs prescription for 95% CL exclusion limits\\n3. HistFitter package with Gaussian nuisance parameters for systematic uncertainties\\n4. Maximum-likelihood (profile likelihood) fit with Poisson/Gaussian terms and Beeston-Barlow-lite MC-stat nuisances\\n5. Poisson statistical modelling with Gaussian-constrained nuisance parameters\\n6. Pseudo-experiment-based calculation of limits and discovery p-values\\n7. Shape-fit approach using mutually exclusive kinematic bins\\n\\nThese methods are documented in the paper.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}", "answered": true, "papers": ["2006.05880", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2106.01676", "2211.08028", "2401.05299", "2407.10549"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids