{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-ca9a57b6", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which statistical methods does analysis 2107.12553 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2107.12553 uses the following statistical methods:\n\n1. **Binned maximum likelihood fit** for SUSY signal strength, background yields, and nuisance parameters.\n2. **Modified frequentist CLs method with asymptotic formulation** at 95% confidence level.\n\nThese methods are used to analyze the data and draw conclusions from the results. \n\nHere are the supporting quotes from the paper:\n\n1. For the binned maximum likelihood fit:\n   - \"A binned maximum likelihood fit is performed to determine the SUSY signal strength, background yields, and nuisance parameters.\"\n\n2. For the modified frequentist CLs method:\n   - \"The modified frequentist CLs method with asymptotic formulation is used to set upper limits on the signal cross-section at 95% confidence level.\"\n\nAnswered from the graph.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2107.12553", "2209.07327", "2604.27044"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2107.12553"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 2, "error": null, "seconds": 0.034}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:binned-ml-fit", "hepkg:method:cls-asymptotic"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:3e413ce6f0a1fcb678a7c849", "hepkg:evidence:6f8590952c765a4ba62fb5dc"], "seen_values": ["2107.12553", "95", "and", "asymptotic", "background", "binned", "cls", "fit", "for", "formulation", "frequentist", "hepkg:method:binned-ml-fit", "hepkg:method:cls-asymptotic", "likelihood", "maximum", "method", "modified", "nuisance", "parameters", "result_uses_statistical_method", "signal", "statistical_method", "strength", "susy", "with", "yields"], "verification_score": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": [], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 7010, "completion_tokens": 216, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 9.40065643703565, "error": ""}, "scores": {"seconds": 9.40065643703565, "llm_calls": 2.0, "tokens": 7226.0, "rounds": 2.0, "errored": 0.0, "answered": 1.0, "abstained": 0.0, "refused_in_text": 0.0, "refusal_flag_disagrees": 0.0, "faithfulness": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": 0.0, "retrieved_label_recall": 1.0, "retrieved_entities": 2.0, "mentioned_label_recall": 0.5, "truncation_loss_labels": 0.5, "tool_calls": 1.0, "tool_errors": 0.0, "tool_error_rate": 0.0, "retrieved_first": 1.0, "entities_retrieved": 2.0, "evidence_quotes": 2.0}}
{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-cb265561", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many object selection requirements does analysis 2407.10549 define?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2407.10549 defines 16 object selection requirements. These include criteria such as '2.5 < |η| < 4.5, pT > 30 GeV', 'D_Xbb tagged: 50% efficient operating point for selecting Higgs bosons with pT > 250 GeV, multijet rejection factor ~110', and others detailed above.", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2407.10549"], "predicate": "object_has_selection"}, "rows": 15, "error": null, "seconds": 0.037}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": [], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:0031a7733212ecdc2d95d720", "hepkg:evidence:12323d7f1d4d9eaa44a2144f", "hepkg:evidence:219e030072e483a7948d38df", "hepkg:evidence:245f20851f8711110019091a", "hepkg:evidence:2a961226e073eeab21e47c6b", "hepkg:evidence:4a7d4ada69c4ff38d7fe451c", "hepkg:evidence:5a216493eb8c0473ee885597", "hepkg:evidence:5c665bc39563070f2844bbee", "hepkg:evidence:8a7fd1adefbe2adb90e2b9d3", "hepkg:evidence:b9b5a552e1eede193356d3c7", "hepkg:evidence:be133f685ec735105d4c6f0d", "hepkg:evidence:bf68ad841d3706d06c074769", "hepkg:evidence:c230daf2a88d2411dd54a78e", "hepkg:evidence:f3f9911bb824eebdcab820e8", "hepkg:evidence:fd477d7e8b71ee32e8c9c04b"], "seen_values": ["0.2", "1", "10", "11", "110", "2", "2.4", "2.47", "2.5", "20", "200", "2407.10549", "25", "250", "3", "30", "4.5", "5", "50", "6", "60", "77", "according", "algorithm", "and", "anti-kt", "applied", "associated-track-based", "b-tagged", "bosons", "calibrated", "channel", "computed", "criteria", "d_xbb", "deltar", "discriminant", "dl1r", "down", "efficiency", "efficient", "electron", "eta", "event", "factor", "for", "gev", "good", "higgs", "identifica