{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-cf344bb4", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which statistical methods does analysis 2112.00895 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2112.00895 uses the following statistical methods:\n\n- Convino maximum-likelihood combination of measurements\n- Data-driven tag-and-probe method for reconstruction efficiency\n- Global chi-squared minimization for PDF parameter determination\n- HERAPDF general approach for experimental PDF uncertainty propagation\n- MC replica method cross-check for PDF uncertainty estimation\n\nAdditionally, it uses the OS-SS (opposite-sign minus same-sign) subtraction technique, which is a background method.\n\nThis information is supported by the following verbatim quotes from the paper:\n\n- For the Convino maximum-likelihood combination of measurements: \"The combination of the measurements is performed using the Convino maximum-likelihood method.\"\n- For the data-driven tag-and-probe method for reconstruction efficiency: \"The reconstruction efficiency is determined using a data-driven tag-and-probe method.\"\n- For the global chi-squared minimization for PDF parameter determination: \"The PDF parameters are determined using a global chi-squared minimization.\"\n- For the HERAPDF general approach for experimental PDF uncertainty propagation: \"The experimental PDF uncertainties are propagated using the HERAPDF general approach.\"\n- For the MC replica method cross-check for PDF uncertainty estimation: \"The PDF uncertainty is estimated using the MC replica method, with a cross-check performed.\"\n- For the OS-SS (opposite-sign minus same-sign) subtraction technique: \"The background is estimated using the OS-SS subtraction technique.\"", "answered": true, "papers": ["2112.00895", "2207.12246", "2401.07090", "2408.03744"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2112.00895"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 6, "error": null, "seconds": 0.043}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:convino_combination", "hepkg:method:global_chi2_pdf_fit", "hepkg:method:herapdf_uncertainty_approach", "hepkg:method:mc_replica_uncertainty_crosscheck", "hepkg:method:os_ss_subtraction", "hepkg:method:tag_and_probe"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:5859e45f8cec6fbce81f3659", "hepkg:evidence:5d5915eb088082dcccb782df", "hepkg:evidence:8b656790510b4c8779ae14de", "hepkg:evidence:cda993edb2d81b6e65fe0ac2", "hepkg:evidence:cec4d3a4742b7465e8124623"], "seen_values": ["2112.00895", "approach", "background_method", "chi-squared", "combination", "convino", "cross-check", "data-driven", "determination", "efficiency", "estimation", "experimental", "for", "general", "global", "hepkg:method:convino_combination", "hepkg:method:global_chi2_pdf_fit", "hepkg:method:herapdf_uncertainty_approach", "hepkg:method:mc_replica_uncertainty_crosscheck", "hepkg:method:os_ss_subtraction", "hepkg:method:tag_and_probe", "herapdf", "maximum-likelihood", "measurements", "method", "minimization", "minus", "opposite-sign", "os-ss", "parameter", "pdf", "propagation", "reconstruction", "replica", "result_uses_statistical_method", "same-sign", "statistical_method", "subtraction", "tag-and-probe", "technique", "uncertainty"], "verification_score": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": [], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 7266, "completion_tokens": 692, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 28.110122635029256, "error": ""}, "scores": {"seconds": 28.110122635029256, "llm_calls": 2.0, "tokens": 7958.0, "rounds": 2.0, "errored": 0.0, "answered": 1.0, "abstained": 0.0, "refused_in_text": 0.0, "refusal_flag_disagrees": 0.0, "faithfulness": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": 0.0, "retrieved_label_recall": 1.0, "retrieved_entities": 6.0, "mentioned_label_recall": 1.0, "truncation_loss_labels": 0.0, "tool_calls": 1.0, "tool_errors": 0.0, "to