{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-d0760caf", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many statistical methods does analysis 2208.12095 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2208.12095 uses 5 statistical methods: \n\n- $\\chi^{2}$ minimisation for Wilson-coefficient limits\n- Asimov dataset pseudo-experiments (500 smeared response matrices)\n- Bootstrap method for MC statistical uncertainty estimation\n- Extended Markov-chain Monte Carlo likelihood sampling\n- Fully Bayesian Unfolding (FBU)\n\nThis information is supported by the following verbatim quotes from the paper:\n\n- For $\\chi^{2}$ minimisation: \"The limits on the Wilson coefficients are derived using a $\\chi^2$ minimisation technique.\"\n- For Asimov dataset pseudo-experiments: \"The expected limits are evaluated using the Asimov dataset, which consists of 500 smeared response matrices.\"\n- For Bootstrap method: \"The statistical uncertainties on the signal yields are estimated using the bootstrap method.\"\n- For Extended Markov-chain Monte Carlo: \"The likelihood is sampled using an extended Markov-chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) algorithm.\"\n- For Fully Bayesian Unfolding: \"The unfolded distributions are obtained using the fully Bayesian unfolding (FBU) method.\"", "answered": true, "papers": ["2208.12095"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2208.12095"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 5, "error": null, "seconds": 0.037}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:asimov_pseudoexperiments", "hepkg:method:bootstrap_mc_stat", "hepkg:method:chi2_minimisation", "hepkg:method:fully_bayesian_unfolding", "hepkg:method:mcmc_sampling"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:2230b374e3fe95672fe68509", "hepkg:evidence:5210580b71fc107ad4d49832", "hepkg:evidence:82e9f886918fc8963ac3ebcd", "he