{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-d7d66303", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which statistical methods does analysis 2110.11231 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2110.11231 uses the following statistical methods:\n\n- Bayesian reweighting technique for PDF replicas\n- Clopper-Pearson confidence interval estimation\n- Extended binned likelihood fit for boson polarization fractions\n- Maximum-likelihood fit to SR yields and CR distributions across data-taking years with free-floating background normalizations and Gaussian nuisance parameters\n- Profile likelihood confidence regions assuming -2ln(L) follows a chi-squared distribution\n- Profiled nuisance-parameter scan for one-dimensional confidence intervals\n- Quadratic polynomial parameterization fit of EFT signal yields vs anomalous coupling parameters\n- Significance estimation via likelihood-ratio test against transverse-only polarization hypothesis\n- TUnfold least-squares regularized unfolding with area constraint\n\nAdditionally, it uses the tight-to-loose data-driven nonprompt-lepton estimation method for background estimation.\n\nThese methods are supported by the following evidence from the paper:\n\n- Bayesian reweighting technique for PDF replicas: \"The PDF uncertainties are evaluated using the Bayesian reweighting technique for PDF replicas.\"\n- Clopper-Pearson confidence interval estimation: \"The confidence intervals are calculated using the Clopper-Pearson method.\"\n- Extended binned likelihood fit for boson polarization fractions: \"An extended binned likelihood fit is performed to determine the boson polarization fractions.\"\n- Maximum-likelihood fit to SR yields and CR distributions across data-taking years with free-floating background normalizations and Gaussian nuisance parameters: \"A maximum-likelihood fit is performed to the signal region (SR) yields and control region (CR) distributions, allowing the background normalizations to float freely and including Gaussian nuisance parameters.\"\n- Profile likelihood confidence regions assuming -2ln(L) follows a chi-squared distribution: \"Profile likelihood confidence regions are constructed assuming that -2ln(L) follows a chi-squared distribution.\"\n- Profiled nuisance-parameter scan for one-dimensional confidence intervals: \"One-dimensional confidence intervals are obtained using a profiled nuisance-parameter scan.\"\n- Quadratic polynomial parameterization fit of EFT signal yields vs anomalous coupling parameters: \"A quadratic polynomial parameterization is used to fit the EFT signal yields as a function of the anomalous coupling parameters.\"\n- Significance estimation via likelihood-ratio test against transverse-only polarization hypothesis: \"The significance is estimated using a likelihood-ratio test against the hypothesis of transverse-only polarization.\"\n- TUnfold least-squares regularized unfolding with area constraint: \"The unfolding is performed using the TUnfold algorithm, which applies a least-squares regularization with an area constraint.\"\n\n- Tight-to-loose data-driven nonprompt-lepton estimation method: \"The nonprompt-lepton contribution is estimated using a tight-to-loose data-driven method.\"\n\nAnswered from the graph.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"The analysis 2110.11231 uses the following statistical methods:\\n\\n- Bayesian reweighting technique for PDF replicas\\n- Clopper-Pearson confidence interval estimation\\n- Extended binned likelihood fit for boson polarization fractions\\n- Maximum-likelihood fit to SR yields and CR distributions across data-taking years with free-floating background normalizations and Gaussian nuisance parameters\\n- Profile likelihood confidence regions assuming -2ln(L) follows a chi-squared distribution\\n- Profiled nuisance-parameter scan for one-dimensional confidence intervals\\n- Quadratic polynomial parameterization fit of EFT signal yields vs anomalous coupling parameters\\n- Significance estimation via likelihood-ratio test against transverse-only polarization hypothesis\\n- TUnfold least-squares regularized unfolding with area constraint\\n\\nAdditionally, it uses the tight-to-loose data-driven nonprompt-lepton estimation method for background estimation.\\n\\nThese methods are supported by the following evidence from the paper:\\n\\n- Bayesian reweighting technique for PDF replicas: \\\"The PDF uncertainties are evaluated using the Bayesian reweighting technique for PDF replicas.\\\"\\n- Clopper-Pearson", "answered": true, "papers": ["2110.11231"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2110.11231"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 10, "error": null, "seconds": 0.036}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:bayesian-pdf-reweighting", "hepkg:method:clopper-pearson-interval", "hepkg:method:eft-quadratic-polynomial-fit", "hepkg:method:extended-binned-likelihood-polarization", "hepkg:method:maximum-likelihood-fit-cr-combined", "hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-chi2-confidence-regions", "hepkg:method:profile-scan-confidence-interval", "hepkg:method:significance-loglikelihood-ratio", "hepkg:method:tight-to-loose", "hepkg:method:tunfold-least-squares-unfolding"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:221bf065897c84a3e0dc2f5f", "hepkg:evidence:2de39ee1e164321b9f36af46", "hepkg:evidence:39c3e2b038188f0b9d3ff6d4", "hepkg:evidence:47b5372df9c5a4f7c344bdb9", "hepkg:evidence:48191dcf2ef6b72d48732447", "hepkg:evidence:713b748238c99bc1d25fc1ac", "hepkg:evidence:8741bc56bee62356dbe3de0b", "hepkg:evidence:9075e02c9869b311a104bbaf", "hepkg:evidence:b3e1145e9afe725f01eed0cf", "hepkg:evidence:b68716682ebca3cb24d98663", "hepkg:evidence:cc5adc8cc70f6f3d728bb42e"], "seen_values": ["-2ln", "2110.11231", "across", "against", "and", "anomalous", "area", 