{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-d8325de9", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which simulated samples does analysis 2012.03799 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2012.03799 uses the following simulated samples:\n\n- $V$+jets sample (Sherpa 2.2.1)\n- Alternative W+jets sample generated with MadGraph for generator-modelling systematics\n- Alternative ttbar sample (MadGraph5_aMC@NLO + Pythia 8) for modelling systematics\n- Alternative ttbar sample (Powheg-Box + Herwig 7) for hadronisation systematics\n- Diboson ($VV$) background sample (Sherpa 2.2.1/2.2.2)\n- Multi-leg LO ttbar, Wt and WWbb samples (MadGraph) for ttbar-Wt interference uncertainty\n- Multiboson sample (Sherpa 2.2.1-2.2.2)\n- Nominal $t\\bar{t}$ MC sample (Powheg Box v2+Pythia 8.230)\n- SUSY stop-pair signal sample (MadGraph 2.6.2 + Pythia 8)\n- Single-top s- and Wt-channel sample (Powheg-Box v2 + Pythia 8)\n- Single-top t-channel sample (Powheg-Box v1 + Pythia 8)\n- Spin-0 mediator dark-matter signal sample (MadGraph 2.6.2 + Pythia 8)\n- ttbar+V sample (MG5_aMC@NLO 2.3.3 + Pythia 8)\n\nThese samples are used to simulate various processes and backgrounds in the analysis.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2010.14293", "2012.03799", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2407.10549"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2012.03799"], "predicate": "result_uses_sample"}, "rows": 13, "error": null, "seconds": 0.041}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:sample:diboson-sherpa", "hepkg:sample:dm-signal", "hepkg:sample:multiboson-sherpa", "hepkg:sample:singletop-swt-channel", "hepkg:sample:singletop-tchannel", "hepkg:sample:susy-signal", "hepkg:sample:ttbar-alt-mg5-pythia8", "hepkg:sample:ttbar-alt-powheg-herwig7", "hepkg:sample:ttbar-nominal", "hepkg:sample:ttbar-wt-wwbb-interference-mg-lo", "hepkg:sample:ttba