{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-d91da3da", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which background-estimation methods does analysis 2202.08676 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2202.08676 uses the following background-estimation methods:\n\n- Data-driven matrix method\n- Gamma function modeling of statistical uncertainties in signal and background estimates\n- Goodness-of-fit test based on the saturated model method\n- Log-normal nuisance parameter modeling of systematic uncertainties in the likelihood\n- Modified frequentist CLs approach with binned profile likelihood test statistic (asymptotic approximation)\n- Simplified likelihood framework for reinterpretation of results\n\nThese methods are used to estimate backgrounds and perform statistical analyses in the paper. \n\nAnswered from the graph.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2202.08676 uses the following background-estimation methods:\\n\\n- Data-driven matrix method\\n- Gamma function modeling of statistical uncertainties in signal and background estimates\\n- Goodness-of-fit test based on the saturated model method\\n- Log-normal nuisance parameter modeling of systematic uncertainties in the likelihood\\n- Modified frequentist CLs approach with binned profile likelihood test statistic (asymptotic approximation)\\n- Simplified likelihood framework for reinterpretation of results\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": ["2106.01676", "2202.08676", "2209.07327", "2307.01094"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2202.08676"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 6, "error": null, "seconds": 0.034}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:cls-profile-likelihood", "hepkg:method:gamma-funct