{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-e242fd0f", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2207.00348 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2207.00348 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- $E_{\\text{T}}^{\\text{miss}}$ soft-term reconstruction uncertainty\n- Background $m_{\\gamma\\gamma}$ modelling uncertainty (spurious signal)\n- Electron energy and momentum scale/resolution uncertainty\n- Electron reconstruction, identification and isolation efficiency uncertainty\n- Heavy-flavour jet radiation modelling uncertainty in non-$t\\bar{t}H$ processes (100% conservative)\n- Higgs boson mass uncertainty (125.09 ± 0.24 GeV)\n- H→γγ branching ratio uncertainty (2.9%)\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- Jet energy scale and resolution uncertainty\n- Jet-vertex-tagger efficiency uncertainty\n- Matrix-element/generator modelling uncertainty (nominal vs MadGraph5_aMC@NLO alternative)\n- Missing higher-order QCD (renormalization/factorization scale) uncertainty\n- Muon energy and momentum scale/resolution uncertainty\n- Muon reconstruction, identification and isolation efficiency uncertainty\n- PDF and $\\alpha_S$ uncertainty\n- Parton shower, underlying event and hadronization modelling uncertainty (Pythia8 vs Herwig7)\n- Photon energy resolution uncertainty\n- Photon energy scale uncertainty\n- Photon identification efficiency uncertainty\n- Photon isolation efficiency uncertainty\n- Pile-up modelling uncertainty\n- b tagging efficiency uncertainty\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the analysis.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2103.04956", "2106.01676", "2109.13808", "2110.11231", "2111.08340", "2202.08676", "2206.09466", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08