{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-e508e935", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many statistical methods does analysis 2004.04545 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2004.04545 uses the following statistical methods:\n\n1. **CLs method** used to derive the 95% CL upper limit on the tH production rate.\n2. **Goodness-of-fit test** assessing compatibility between the observed \\( m_{\\gamma\\gamma} \\) spectra and the fit model.\n3. **Profile likelihood ratio** used as the test statistic, with the asymptotic approximation used for statistical interpretation.\n4. **Simultaneous maximum-likelihood fit** to the \\( m_{\\gamma\\gamma} \\) spectra in all categories.\n\nTherefore, the analysis uses **4 statistical methods**.\n\nHere are the supporting quotes from the paper:\n\n- \"CLs method used to derive the 95% CL upper limit on the tH production rate\"\n- \"Goodness-of-fit test assessing compatibility between the observed \\( m_{\\gamma\\gamma} \\) spectra and the fit model\"\n- \"Profile likelihood ratio used as the test statistic, with the asymptotic approximation used for statistical interpretation\"\n- \"Simultaneous maximum-likelihood fit to the \\( m_{\\gamma\\gamma} \\) spectra in all categories\"\n\nAnswered from the graph.", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2004.04545"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 4, "error": null, "seconds": 0.045}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": [], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:0afa77fb00c7b240c0486454", "hepkg:evidence:1a8aecfbbc34e9d65853ace6", "hepkg:evidence:508c7ae8db663a38fe18fbd0", "hepkg:evidence:d5209575193a0eb3fb86d5f7"], "seen_values": ["2004.04545", "95", "all", "and", "approximation", "assessing", "asymptotic", "between", "categories", "cls", "compatibility", "derive", "fit", "for", "goodness-of-fit", "interpretation", "likelihood", "limit", "m_gammagamma", "maximum-likelihood", "method", "model", "none", "observed", "production", "profile", "rate", "ratio", "result_uses_statistical_method", "simultaneous", "spectra", "statistic", "statistical", "test", "the", "upper", "used", "with"], "verification_score": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": [], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 7119, "completion_tokens": 291, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 12.28397093899548, "error": ""}, "scores": {"seconds": 12.28397093899548, "llm_calls": 2.0, "tokens": 7410.0, "rounds": 2.0, "errored": 0.0, "answered": 1.0, "abstained": 0.0, "refused_in_text": 0.0, "refusal_flag_disagrees": 0.0, "faithfulness": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": 0.0, "count_correct": 1.0, "tool_calls": 1.0, "tool_errors": 0.0, "tool_error_rate": 0.0, "retrieved_first": 1.0, "entities_retrieved": 0.0, "evidence_quotes": 4.0}}
