{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-e59e7835", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2602.18611 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2602.18611 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- Background parametrization choice uncertainty (spurious signal, unconstrained)\n- Double-b tagger efficiency uncertainty\n- Higgs boson branching fraction prediction uncertainty\n- Integrated luminosity measurement uncertainty (year-by-year, 2016-2018)\n- Jet energy resolution (JER) uncertainty\n- Jet energy scale (JES) uncertainty\n- Lepton efficiency and energy scale uncertainty (tag-and-probe on Z resonance)\n- Limited size of simulated (MC) samples uncertainty\n- Missing higher-order QCD corrections uncertainty (signal)\n- Missing transverse momentum (p_T^miss) uncertainty\n- PDF modelling uncertainty (CT14, MMHT2014 vs NNPDF3.0 replicas)\n- Pileup modelling uncertainty\n- Strong coupling constant (alpha_S) uncertainty\n- Underlying event and parton shower modelling uncertainty\n- b tagging efficiency uncertainty\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the analysis as potential sources of systematic error.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"The analysis 2602.18611 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\\n\\n- Background parametrization choice uncertainty (spurious signal, unconstrained)\\n- Double-b tagger efficiency uncertainty\\n- Higgs boson branching fraction prediction uncertainty\\n- Integrated luminosity measurement uncertainty (year-by-year, 2016-2018)\\n- Jet energy resolution (JER) uncertainty\\n- Jet energy scale (JES) uncertainty\\n- Lepton efficiency and energy scale uncertainty (tag-and-probe on Z resonance)\\n- Limited size of simulated (MC) samples uncertainty\\n- Missing higher-order QCD corrections uncertai