{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-ed117d3e", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which statistical methods does analysis 2202.08676 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2202.08676 uses the following statistical methods:\n\n- Data-driven matrix method\n- Gamma function modeling of statistical uncertainties in signal and background estimates\n- Goodness-of-fit test based on the saturated model method\n- Log-normal nuisance parameter modeling of systematic uncertainties in the likelihood\n- Modified frequentist CLs approach with binned profile likelihood test statistic (asymptotic approximation)\n- Simplified likelihood framework for reinterpretation of results\n\nThese methods were retrieved from the paper's content in the graph.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2106.01676", "2202.08676", "2209.07327", "2307.01094"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2202.08676"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 6, "error": null, "seconds": 0.037}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:cls-profile-likelihood", "hepkg:method:gamma-function-stat-uncertainty", "hepkg:method:goodness-of-fit-saturated-model", "hepkg:method:lognormal-nuisance-parameters", "hepkg:method:matrix-method", "hepkg:method:simplified-likelihood-reinterpretation"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:1082eff101f70931a38a51da", "hepkg:evidence:3bd01e9413f948f9359c6257", "hepkg:evidence:6026d72d040e78aa2cfb915f", "hepkg:evidence:787ec4395af1b651d0749ae6", "hepkg:evidence:97a73217bd6c32652227b368", "hepkg:evidence:a6c8eadca8ad1413e3ee6d3c"], "seen_values": ["2202.08676", "and", "approach", "approximation", "asymptotic", "background", "background_method", "based", "binned", "cls", "data-driven", "estimates", "for", "framework", "frequentist", "function", "gamma", "goodness-of-fit", "h