{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-eece413e", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many object selection requirements does analysis 2112.03161 define?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2112.03161 defines 16 object selection requirements. Here are some examples:\n\n- \"DL channel: second (subleading) lepton pT > 10 GeV\"\n- \"pT > 27 GeV (baseline requirement, at least one electron OR muon in the event)\"\n- \"pT > 30 GeV (baseline requirement, at least one electron OR muon in the event)\"\n- \"pT > 200 GeV\"\n- \"pT > 30 GeV and identified with DeepJet tagger at working point of ~80% efficiency for b jets and ~1% misidentification for light-flavor quark and gluon jets\"\n- \"p_T^miss > 85 GeV\"\n\nAnd more detailed selections for specific objects and regions.", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2112.03161"], "predicate": "object_has_selection"}, "rows": 15, "error": null, "seconds": 0.037}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": [], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:0b227384ea4c9afeb4b93ed3", "hepkg:evidence:425b3d51efbc7994dcfdbd23", "hepkg:evidence:4f488e85c778bd16f6b5a7c5", "hepkg:evidence:57ecba77542860829a07ff64", "hepkg:evidence:5c415f39a1034ae5d21ff456", "hepkg:evidence:7c8878566ca8803d2d657cea", "hepkg:evidence:90ab8a50380fdff628c1a6b7", "hepkg:evidence:93bdcbe74a87c588846f28e1", "hepkg:evidence:b0e8ce48dee2629b9f98cede", "hepkg:evidence:bf67807ed84b760916f4fe24", "hepkg:evidence:c33cc870d61571dbeaab892a", "hepkg:evidence:c725ee6d49042e320ce336a4", "hepkg:evidence:c7eeed15b588f36b5c06c5fb"], "seen_values": ["0.75", "0.8", "0.97", "1", "1.2", "1.479", "1.6", "10", "11", "11.0", "2", "2.0", "2.4", "2.5", "20", "200", "2112.03161", "27", "3", "30", "5", "50", "8", "80", "85", "ak4", "ak8", "and", "applied", "barrel", "baseline", "bb