{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-f1fe035d", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which background-estimation methods does analysis 2405.18661 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2405.18661 uses the following background-estimation methods:\n\n- 95% CL upper limit setting on Higgs boson pair production cross section and self-coupling\n- Angular weighting method using event weights functions of rapidity and cos(theta*) for acceptance-corrected AFB\n- Combination of CMS and ATLAS 7/8 TeV measurements exploiting complementary systematic uncertainties\n- Combination of individual production/decay-mode results via signal strength parameters using published statistical methodology\n- Combined PDF and alpha_S fit of CMS and HERA data (or profiling of a global PDF set)\n- Combined fit to MVA output distributions in categories of jet and b jet multiplicity\n- Fit of expected trigonometric angular distributions to extract polarization fractions\n- Fit parameterizing contributions of different CKM matrix elements to single top production and decay\n- Fit to MVA discriminator output (or ancillary kinematic variables) across event categories\n- Integration of published differential jet cross sections accounting for bin-to-bin systematic correlations\n- MVA discriminators trained to separate tttt signal from backgrounds, combined fit across categories\n- Signal-background separation via a robust kinematic variable or a multivariate-analysis (MVA) approach\n- Simplified template cross sections (STXS) minimal merging scheme fit per production-mode kinematic bin\n- Simultaneous extraction of alpha_S with the gluon PDF fit\n- Simultaneous fit of ttbar cross section and b-tagging efficiency using binomial dependency on b-tagged jet multiplicity\n- Total cross section obtained from integration of each of 22 differential cross section measurements\n- Unfolding procedure correcting for detector resolution/efficiency and PS/hadronization effects to particle or parton level\n\nThese methods are recorded in the graph as the statistical methods used in the analysis.", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2405.18661"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 17, "error": null, "seconds": 0.038}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": [], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:21b4e83f644b9c1e0c17bc49", "hepkg:evidence:309b1a46abc571c8b25ec188", "hepkg:evidence:3889967e947945b6ba405ba7", "hepkg:evidence:3a129f56a43f8b24ccfe66ec", "hepkg:evidence:531d74d0397f9aaeff30f925", "hepkg:evidence:6dcb0b5deae26f1e8241ddc4", "hepkg:evidence:7c87b8a47d8272c03439b846", "hepkg:evidence:bb87abb3d55b334d5a61c211", "hepkg:evidence:bcce6ac3bc2fcfa2d66da7af", "hepkg:evidence:d74dfd3eeaf16453936d7b91", "hepkg:evidence:da92607859d7eb7b4ffd1bad", "hepkg:evidence:dcb4d61d143af0bb5f043567", "hepkg:evidence:eca44fde740f4892adccd87f", "hepkg:evidence:eec08e5e39401e74f5b6d7b4"], "seen_values": ["22", "2405.18661", "7", "8", "95", "acceptance-corrected", "accounting", "across", "afb", "alpha_s", "ancillary", "and", "angular", "approach", "atlas", "b-tagged", "b-tagging", "backgrounds", "bin", "bin-to-bin", "binomial", "boson", "categories", "ckm", "cms", "combination", "combined", "complementary", "contributions", "correcting", "correlations", "cos", "cross", "data", "decay", "decay-mode", "dependency", "detector", "different", "differential", "discriminator", "discriminators", "distributions", "each", "effects", "efficiency", "elements", "event", "expected", "exploiting", "extract", "extraction", "fit", "for", "fractions", "from", "functions", "global", "gluon", "hadronization", "hera", "higgs", "individual", "integration", "jet", "kinematic", "level", "limit", "matrix", "measurements", "merging", "method", "methodology", "minimal", "multiplicity", 