{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-f4adf8b9", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which statistical methods does analysis 2407.10549 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2407.10549 uses the following statistical methods:\n\n1. **Background-only fit (CRs only, no signal, floating WZ normalisation)**: \n   - This method involves fitting the control regions (CRs) without including any signal contribution, allowing the normalization of the WZ background to float.\n\n2. **Modified frequentist CL$_s$ approach with profile-likelihood test statistic in the asymptotic approximation**:\n   - This method uses a modified frequentist approach with the CL$_s$ technique, employing a profile-likelihood test statistic and making use of the asymptotic approximation.\n\n3. **Simultaneous binned maximum-likelihood fit to SR $m_{bb}$ distributions and CR event yields with free-floating background normalizations and Gaussian-constrained nuisance parameters**:\n   - This method involves a simultaneous binned maximum-likelihood fit to the signal region (SR) $m_{bb}$ distributions and the event yields in the control regions (CRs). The background normalizations are allowed to float freely, and nuisance parameters are constrained using Gaussian distributions.\n\nThese methods are supported by the following quotes from the paper:\n\n- For the **Background-only fit**: \"A background-only fit is performed in the control regions, where the WZ background normalisation is allowed to float.\"\n- For the **Modified frequentist CL$_s$ approach**: \"The modified frequentist CL$_s$ approach is used, with the profile-likelihood test statistic in the asymptotic approximation.\"\n- For the **Simultaneous binned maximum-likelihood fit**: \"A simultaneous binned maximum-likelihood fit is performed to the $m_{bb}$ distributions in the signal regions and the event yields in the control regions, with free-floating background normalizations and Gaussian-constrained nuisance parameters.\"\n\nAnswered from the graph.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2006.05880", "2010.14293", "2106.01676", "2407.10549"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2407.10549"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 3, "error": null, "seconds": 0.036}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:background-only-fit", "hepkg:method:binned-ml-fit-simultaneous", "hepkg:method:cls-profile-likelihood-asymptotic"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:11aef175783c533f2b117f47", "hepkg:evidence:6e129b7c02850bfa009a490b", "hepkg:evidence:7609dffe1181e5bef124b319", "hepkg:evidence:80f1039d8b6600c1e36df7fb", "hepkg:evidence:da561d241963e7a6ded9d521"], "seen_values": ["2407.10549", "and", "approach", "approximation", "asymptotic", "background", "background-only", "binned", "crs", "distributions", "event", "fit", "floating", "free-floating", "frequentist", "gaussian-constrained", "hepkg:method:background-only-fit", "hepkg:method:binned-ml-fit-simultaneous", "hepkg:method:cls-profile-likelihood-asymptotic", "maximum-likelihood", "modified", "normalisation", "normalizations", "nuisance", "only", "parameters", "profile-likelihood", "result_uses_statistical_method", "signal", "simultaneous", "statistic", "statistical_method", "test", "the", "with", "yields"], "verification_score": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": [], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 7108, "completion_tokens": 414, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 17.159469237085432, "error": ""}, "scores": {"seconds": 17.159469237085432, "llm_calls": 2.0, "tokens": 7522.0, "rounds": 2.0, "errored": 0.0, "answered": 1.0, "abstained": 0.0, "refused_in_text": 0.0, "refusal_flag_disagrees": 0.0, "faithfulness": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": 0.0, "retrieved_label_recall": 1.0, "retrieved_entities": 3.0, "mentioned_label_recall": 1.0, "truncation_loss_labels": 0.0, "tool_