{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-f6b04322", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2309.14442 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2309.14442 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- Colour reconnection model uncertainty\n- Electron reconstruction and identification efficiency uncertainty\n- Factorization scale (μF) uncertainty\n- Finite simulated MC sample size (Barlow-Beeston-like) uncertainty\n- Inclusive ttC cross section normalization uncertainty (20%)\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- Jet energy resolution (JER) uncertainty\n- Jet energy scale (JES) uncertainty\n- L1 ECAL/muon prefiring correction uncertainty\n- ME-PS matching (hdamp) uncertainty\n- Muon reconstruction and identification uncertainty\n- Parton distribution function (PDF) uncertainty\n- Parton shower scale uncertainty: final-state radiation (FSR)\n- Parton shower scale uncertainty: initial-state radiation (ISR)\n- Pileup reweighting uncertainty\n- Renormalization scale (μR) uncertainty\n- Top quark pT reweighting/modelling uncertainty\n- Trigger efficiency scale factor uncertainty\n- Underlying event modeling (CP5 tune parameter) uncertainty\n- b quark fragmentation modelling uncertainty\n- b tagging (and mistag) efficiency calibration uncertainty\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the analysis 2309.14442.\n\nAnswered from the graph.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.14060", "2007.02873", "2012.01581", "2012.03799", "2103.06956", "2111.08340", "2112.00895", "2112.03161", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2303.15340", "2309.14442", "2402.08486", "2408.03744", "2503.19420", "2506.13565", "2509.22535"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2309.14442"], "predicate": "result_has_systematic"}, "rows": 21, "erro