{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-fe9cff45", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many object selection requirements does analysis 2106.01676 define?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2106.01676 defines 16 object selection requirements. Here are some examples:\n\n- Exactly three baseline leptons required\n- Exactly three signal leptons required\n- Tight isolation working point\n- Multivariate b-tagging discriminant applied for \\(|\\eta| < 2.5\\); working point at 85% b-tagging efficiency (rejection factor 2.7 for c-jets, 25 for light/gluon jets)\n- Non-prompt lepton BDT used to tighten requirements on the lowest-\\(p_T\\) lepton\n- \\(p_T > 25 \\, \\text{GeV}; |\\eta| < 2.37\\) excluding \\(1.37 < |\\eta| < 1.52\\); Tight identification\n\nThese selections are crucial for defining the objects used in the analysis. \n\nAnswered from the graph.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2106.01676 defines 16 object selection requirements. Here are some examples:\\n\\n- Exactly three baseline leptons required\\n- Exactly three signal leptons required\\n- Tight isolation working point\\n- Multivariate b-tagging discriminant applied for \\(|\\\\eta| < 2.5\\); working point at 85% b-tagging efficiency (rejection factor 2.7 for c-jets, 25 for light/gluon jets)\\n- Non-prompt lepton BDT used to tighten requirements on the lowest-\\(p_T\\) lepton\\n- \\(p_T > 25 \\\\, \\\\text{GeV}; |\\\\eta| < 2.37\\) excluding \\(1.37 < |\\\\eta| < 1.52\\); Tight identification\\n\\nThese selections are crucial for defining the objects used in the analysis.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2106.01676"], "predicate": "object_has_selection"}, "rows": 16, "error":