{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-feec4b57", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2106.01676 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2106.01676 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- $t\\bar{t}$ initial- and final-state radiation modelling uncertainty\n- Cross-section normalisation uncertainty for minor backgrounds (ttbarW 13%, ttbarZ 12%, ttbarh 10%, triboson 20%, other rare top 50%)\n- Data-driven Z+jets fake-factor estimation uncertainty (statistical, parameterisation, non-Z+jets subtraction)\n- E_T^miss modelling uncertainty (object scales + soft-term resolution/scale)\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- Jet energy scale (JES) and jet energy resolution (JER) uncertainty\n- MC background sample statistical (limited-event) uncertainty\n- PDF and alpha_S uncertainty\n- QCD renormalisation and factorisation scale uncertainty (three Gaussian nuisance parameters)\n- SUSY signal acceptance uncertainty (renormalisation/factorisation/CKKW-L matching scales, Pythia8 shower tune), 5%-20%\n- Trigger, flavour-tagging, JVT and lepton reconstruction/identification/impact-parameter/isolation efficiency uncertainties\n- WZ/ZZ resummation, ME-PS matching and PS recoil scheme uncertainty (Sherpa parameter variation)\n- ttbar ME/PS modelling uncertainty (Powheg vs MadGraph5_aMC@NLO, Pythia8 vs Herwig7)\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the analysis.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2103.04956", "2106.01676", "2109.13808", "2111.08340", "2202.08676", "2205.05120", "2206.09466", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2307.01094", "2308.02285", "2312.04450", "2401.05299", "2402.08486", "2407.10549", "2503.19420", "2506.13565", "