{"run_id": "20260803T113606-hepkg", "qid": "gen-paper-ffc9d525", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "How many region selection requirements does analysis 2401.05299 define?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2401.05299 defines 14 region selection requirements. Here are the details:\n\n1. Exactly three particle-level leptons with total charge ±1, same-sign pair p_T >= 20 GeV each.\n2. Exactly two particle-level leptons with the same charge, each p_T >= 20 GeV.\n3. Leading/sub-leading leptons pass TMex, MexT, or MexMex criteria, sub-leading lepton is a muon; leptons pT (20,20) GeV.\n4. Leading/sub-leading leptons pass TMex, MexT, or MexMex criteria, sub-leading lepton is an electron; leptons pT (20,20) GeV.\n5. Loose-tight-tight (LTT) three leptons with p_T (10,20,20) GeV and total lepton charge exactly ±1.\n6. OS-SF pair mass and Z-mass veto: m(l+l-)^SF > 12 GeV, |m(l+l-)^SF - mZ| > 10 GeV, |m_3l - mZ| > 10 GeV.\n7. Three leptons with (L,M,M) definition, p_T (10,20,20) GeV; OS-SF pair compatible with Z boson: |m(l+l-)^SF - mZ| < 10 GeV.\n8. Two tight (TT) same-sign light leptons, each with p_T > 20 GeV.\n9. b-jet multiplicity fitted.\n10. m_T(l0, MET) < 250 GeV for the TMex and MexT sub-regions.\n11. m_ll > 12 GeV & |m_ll - mZ| > 10 GeV for OS-SF pairs; |m_lll - mZ| > 10 GeV.\n12. m_ll > 12 GeV for same-flavour pairs.\n13. μμe* selection: two muons plus one electron identified as a material-conversion candidate, targeting Z→μμγ*(→e+e-) with one electron unreconstructed.\n14. μμe* selection: two muons plus one electron identified as an internal-conversion candidate, targeting Z→μμγ*(→e+e-) with one electron unreconstructed.\n\nThese requirements are supported by the following verbatim quotes from the paper:\n\n- \"Exactly three particle-level leptons with total charge ±1, same-sign pair p_T >= 20 GeV each\"\n- \"Exactly two particle-level leptons with the same charge, each p_T >= 20 GeV\"\n- \"Leading/sub-leading leptons pass TMex, MexT, or MexMex criteria, sub-leading lepton is a muon; leptons pT (20,20) GeV\"\n- \"Leading/sub-leading leptons pass TMex, MexT, or MexMex criteria, sub-leading lepton is an electron; leptons pT (20,20) GeV\"\n- \"Loose-tight-tight (LTT) three leptons with p_T (10,20,20) GeV and total lepton charge exactly ±1\"\n- \"OS-SF pair mass and Z-mass veto: m(l+l-)^SF > 12 GeV, |m(l+l-)^SF - mZ| > 10 GeV, |m_3l - mZ| > 10 GeV\"\n- \"Three leptons with (L,M,M) definition, p_T (10,20,20) GeV; OS-SF pair compatible with Z bos", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2401.05299"], "predicate": "region_has_selection"}, "rows": 14, "error": null, "seconds": 0.066}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": [], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:00c20a72dea6ea0ecbcf1c46", "hepkg:evidence:02eef5e890955112e6e1c81e", "hepkg:evidence:143b5dcd7083bbb76e25e688", "hepkg:evidence:17c71bc408db2b1b2795be80", "hepkg:evidence:1f8968ff07a0e675888f08c4", "hepkg:evidence:214c8a6fa44f9a6b5ebe045a", "hepkg:evidence:3454638cfcb671744a3fe7c9", "hepkg:evidence:38d83cac6f47c7e802061528", "hepkg:evidence:3eaf0cc9e370becf95f808a1", "hepkg:evidence:5f20cf69c841ca6bbfaf2241", "hepkg:evidence:5fbe90598ccf8623311a5791", "hepkg:evidence:98ea3052f71285cb4e2b84a5", "hepkg:evidence:af2d51e78c72fc361e4f48f4", "hepkg:evidence:b79c42fa02494bcd395a1635", "hepkg:evidence:b7fa10e927d119580b145753", "hepkg:evidence:ba52d4e319dfe5aea4baa7e0", "hepkg:evidence:be1d530bb2f5b757b6b58b0d", "hepkg:evidence:be7fee15cc8c47053a99e155", "hepkg:evidence:d8a7622558485ec885de6de5", "hepkg:evidence:d90e15f597be317dd98d650b", "hepkg:evidence:e3a4f158b60b2489549d2f4d", "hepkg:evidence:e78b28504887f278fbd3a56f", "hepkg:evidence:eaf5c2e0fa28b4622577e463", "hepkg:evidence:eb2c4b628b607cef363b3f6f"], "seen_values": ["0", "1", "10", "10,20,20", "10202", "102020", "12", "2", "2